// Built by tools/build-about.py from docs/help/*.md. Do not edit: change the guides and run the script again.
export default {"guides":[{"id":"getting-started","title":"Getting started","summary":[{"s":"What Skald counts, how the sections and tabs are laid out, and how to choose a period, filter, drill down, compare and export."}],"blocks":[{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To look around first, open the "},{"a":"live demo","href":"https://spcaeo.github.io/skald/"},{"s":": the whole dashboard with two months of sample data for a made-up site. No sign-up. Saving and the settings pages need a running Skald, so in the demo they say so."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"New here?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Four short guides take you from nothing to a working install:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"a":"Docker: first install in 10 minutes","href":"#help?part=docker-first-install"},{"s":": run it, sign in, fill the history, check it with the doctor."}],[{"a":"Pick your road","href":"#help?part=pick-your-road"},{"s":": which way your leads and bookings should reach Skald, for your kind of site."}],[{"a":"Send leads from your backend in 5 minutes","href":"#help?part=leads-from-your-backend"},{"s":": the signed lead hook, with copy-paste examples."}],[{"a":"Demo bookings","href":"#help?part=demo-bookings"},{"s":": Calendly and Cal.com, embedded, linked or by webhook, and keeping only your own event types."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"What Skald counts"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald reads your web server's own access log. Every request the server answers is one line in that log, so Skald sees every visit, including the ones a browser script never sees: AI assistants, search engines and bots."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each request lands in exactly one group, and the groups add up to the log exactly:"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Group"}],[{"s":"What is in it"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"People"}],[{"s":"A browser that is none of the groups below"}]],[[{"s":"AI assistants"}],[{"s":"AI crawlers that collect for training, crawlers that index for AI search, fetches made because someone asked a question, and people who followed a link from an AI answer"}]],[[{"s":"Search engines"}],[{"s":"Classic indexing, such as Google and Bing"}]],[[{"s":"Bots and scanners"}],[{"s":"Monitors, SEO tools, link previews from chats, and probes"}]],[[{"s":"Our own"}],[{"s":"Your team, your own crawler and your tests. Kept apart, never counted as people"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Keep three words apart:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Requests"},{"s":" are lines in the log. One page can make many requests."}],[{"b":"People"},{"s":" are browsers that look like real readers. This is an upper bound: when in doubt, a request is not counted as a person."}],[{"b":"Machines"},{"s":" are everything else: AI crawlers, search engines and bots. They are shown in their own units, never added to people."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"AI traffic is not people. A person who clicks a link inside an AI answer is counted as a person, with the AI assistant as their source."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"The optional script tag"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If your site adds the "},{"code":"skald.js"},{"s":" script tag, Skald also counts what happens inside a page: button clicks, form steps, demo bookings, links out, and readers who reach three quarters of a page. These show on "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Events","href":"#sales/events"},{"s":". The log's figures never depend on the tag. See "},{"a":"Tracking script","href":"#help?part=tracking-script"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"The menu"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The sidebar has five sections. Each section has tabs along its top."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Section"}],[{"s":"Tabs"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Overview"}],[{"s":"Summary, Insights"}]],[[{"s":"Traffic"}],[{"s":"Visitors, Sources, Pages, Places & devices, Time"}]],[[{"s":"Leads & sales"}],[{"s":"Pipeline, Bookings, Funnels, Events, People"}]],[[{"s":"AI & bots"}],[{"s":"Assistants, Crawlers, Crawler rules, llms.txt"}]],[[{"s":"Site"}],[{"s":"Health, Alerts, Requests, Not found, Speed, Data quality"}]]]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Overview > Summary"},{"s":" is where every visit starts: the period's headline figures, leads and demos booked among them."}],[{"b":"Overview > Insights"},{"s":" lists what is working, what dropped, and what is new or gone, leads too."}],[{"b":"Traffic"},{"s":" is who came, from where, to which pages, on what, and when."}],[{"b":"Leads & sales"},{"s":" is what the visits brought: leads by stage, demo bookings, funnels, events, and one person's story."}],[{"b":"AI & bots"},{"s":" is AI assistants (the pages they fetch to answer a question, and the visitors they send), crawlers, which crawlers may come in, and your llms.txt."}],[{"b":"Site"},{"s":" is the server: what it answered, open alerts, the request log line by line, pages not found, page speed and the data's own checks."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The address names the section and the tab, for example "},{"code":"#traffic/sources"},{"s":". Older links, such as "},{"code":"#sources"},{"s":" or "},{"code":"#live"},{"s":", still open the right tab."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Two switches sit in the top bar on every page:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Today · Live"},{"s":" sets every tab to today so far, redrawn every 2 minutes. On Overview > Summary it also shows the newest visits and AI events, and today's leads and bookings as they arrive. Turn it off to go back to the period you had."}],[{"b":"Compare with…"},{"s":" puts another period beside this one. See Compare, below."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"When your site reports leads (a form, a booking), they show beside the visitors on Overview > Summary, Traffic > Sources, Traffic > Pages, Traffic > Places & devices and Overview > Insights, not only under Leads & sales. See "},{"a":"Leads on every page","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"b":"Settings"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Help"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"About"},{"s":" sit at the foot of the sidebar. Settings (the gear) has its own menu. See "},{"a":"Settings and retention","href":"#help?part=settings-and-retention"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The round "},{"b":"You"},{"s":" button beside the gear holds your own choices:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Theme"},{"s":": System, Light or Dark."}],[{"b":"Time zone"},{"s":": show times in your own zone, the site's zone, or UTC."}],[{"b":"Your account"},{"s":", "},{"b":"All settings"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Help"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Keyboard shortcuts"},{"s":", "},{"b":"What's new"},{"s":", "},{"b":"About Skald"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"Plain page"},{"s":" (every figure, without scripts)."}],[{"b":"Sign out"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"On a phone, the five sections sit in the bottom bar, and a section's tabs scroll sideways. "},{"b":"Menu"},{"s":" in the bottom bar opens Settings, Help, About and your own choices."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Choosing a period"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The date range sits in the top bar: "},{"b":"Today"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Yesterday"},{"s":", "},{"b":"7 days"},{"s":", "},{"b":"30 days"},{"s":", "},{"b":"90 days"},{"s":" or "},{"b":"Custom"},{"s":". The default is 30 days. Every figure on the page follows the period."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To choose your own dates:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Custom"},{"s":" in the top bar."}],[{"s":"Pick the first day in "},{"b":"From"},{"s":" and the last day in "},{"b":"To"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Days are counted midnight to midnight in the site's own time zone, whatever time zone you choose for display. The site's zone is set in "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Sites"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"A brand-new site has no whole day yet, so it opens on Today."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Whole days and withheld days"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Every figure is counted twice, by two separate roads. A day is shown only when both counts agree."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"A day that is"}],[{"s":"Means"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Whole"}],[{"s":"Both counts agree. It is in every total"}]],[[{"s":"Partial"}],[{"s":"The log covers only part of the day. It is left out of totals"}]],[[{"s":"Withheld"}],[{"s":"The two counts did not add up. Nothing is shown for it"}]],[[{"s":"Not collected"}],[{"s":"Skald was not reading the log that day"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A withheld day is never shown as zero. A figure that was not recorded is left blank, not zero. Unknown stays unknown. When a period holds such days, the page says how many and which."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Today's live figures can be withheld too, if they do not add up. They come back at the next recount."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Filters"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Filters"},{"s":" in the top bar."}],[{"s":"Choose a Country, Page path (contains or starts with), Source, Campaign, Referring site, Device or Browser."}],[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Apply filters"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Active filters show as chips under the top bar. Select the cross on a chip to remove that filter, or "},{"b":"Clear all"},{"s":" in the Filters panel."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The log keeps each breakdown on its own, so filters cannot be crossed (for example, Canada AND Chrome). A filter that a tab cannot apply is greyed out, and the tab says so."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If your site has several page groups (for example, the blog apart from the product pages), a "},{"b":"Page group"},{"s":" list sits beside the period."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Saved views"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Save the period, page group and filters on screen under a name, and come back to them later. Saved views are in the top bar, and in the "},{"b":"More"},{"s":" menu on a narrow screen. The address bar also keeps every choice, so you can share a link. That includes a long list's search, filters, sort and page, such as the request log on Site > Requests."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Find a person"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Owners and admins also have a "},{"b":"Find a person"},{"s":" box in the top bar (a search icon on a narrower screen, and in "},{"b":"Ctrl K"},{"s":"). Type an IP address, an email, a lead or a visitor ID to see that person's visits, leads and conversions. Each search is written to the audit log. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Drill-down"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Select any country, page, source, AI assistant, campaign, referring site, device, browser, hour, address or bot. A panel opens with its trend, the visits and the requests behind it."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Keep selecting inside the panel to narrow further."}],[{"s":"Step back with the browser's Back button, or with the trail at the top of the page."}],[{"s":"On the keyboard, press Enter on a value, a bar or an hour."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"On "},{"a":"Traffic > Pages","href":"#traffic/pages"},{"s":", select a page to see its story: when it was published, its first crawl, its first AI fetch, its first person and its first lead."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Compare"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Compare with…"},{"s":" in the top bar and choose what to put beside the period:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Previous period"},{"s":": the same number of days just before."}],[{"b":"Same period last year"},{"s":": 52 weeks earlier, so the weekdays match."}],[{"b":"Custom period"},{"s":": any whole days you pick, up to 12 months."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Tables then show A (the period in the top bar), B (the one you chose) and the change. Charts show B as a dashed line. A tab that does not compare says so in one line. Previous period and last year compare only when both periods are whole and checked; a custom period counts whole days and names any it left out. "},{"b":"Turn compare off"},{"s":" in the same menu."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"These tabs compare: Overview > Summary, Traffic > Sources, Pages and Places & devices, Leads & sales > Pipeline, AI & bots > Assistants and Crawlers, and Site > Health. Leads, demos booked and every completed action are compared too, when every day of both periods has checked conversions."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Today is never compared: turning on "},{"b":"Today · Live"},{"s":" turns Compare off."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Export"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Export"},{"s":" in the top bar:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Tables on this tab (ZIP)"},{"s":": every table, with the current filters, as CSV files."}],[{"b":"This tab as JSON"},{"s":": the tables and the period's totals."}],[{"b":"Print this tab"},{"s":": a clean report. Choose Save as PDF in the print dialog to keep a PDF."}],[{"b":"Report builder"},{"s":": choose several tabs, the period, page group and filters, then print or download them together."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To read figures from a script or an AI tool, see "},{"a":"API","href":"#help?part=api"},{"s":" and "},{"a":"MCP","href":"#help?part=mcp"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Keyboard shortcuts"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Shortcuts do nothing while you type in a field."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Keys"}],[{"s":"What it does"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"?"}],[{"s":"Show the list of shortcuts"}]],[[{"s":"Ctrl K (Cmd K on a Mac)"}],[{"s":"Command palette: go anywhere, run anything"}]],[[{"s":"/"}],[{"s":"Search the list on this tab"}]],[[{"s":"["}],[{"s":"Shrink the sidebar to icons, or open it again"}]],[[{"s":"Esc"}],[{"s":"Close a panel or a menu"}]],[[{"s":"g then a letter"}],[{"s":"Go to a tab"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Letters to use after "},{"code":"g"},{"s":":"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Letter"}],[{"s":"Tab"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"o, i"}],[{"s":"Overview > Summary, Insights"}]],[[{"s":"l"}],[{"s":"Overview > Summary with Today · Live on"}]],[[{"s":"c"}],[{"s":"Overview > Summary compared with the previous period"}]],[[{"s":"v, s, p, d, t"}],[{"s":"Traffic > Visitors, Sources, Pages, Places & devices, Time"}]],[[{"s":"e, x, f, n"}],[{"s":"Leads & sales > Pipeline, Bookings, Funnels, Events"}]],[[{"s":"b"}],[{"s":"AI & bots > Assistants"}]],[[{"s":"h, a, r, k, w, q"}],[{"s":"Site > Health, Alerts, Requests, Not found, Speed, Data quality"}]],[[{"s":"u"}],[{"s":"Settings > Internal traffic"}]],[[{"s":", (comma)"}],[{"s":"Settings"}]]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Your site on Vercel, Netlify or behind Cloudflare"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald needs a record of every request. A site on your own server has one: its access log. Other hosts keep that log to themselves, so it has to be sent to Skald. Whoever runs your Skald server sets this up once:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Vercel:"},{"s":" a Log Drain sends every request to Skald (Vercel Pro or Enterprise). On the Hobby plan, only the "},{"code":"skald.js"},{"s":" tag works, so Skald sees people but not AI assistants or crawlers. Step by step: "},{"a":"Skald for a site on Vercel","href":"https://github.com/spcaeo/skald/blob/main/docs/VERCEL.md"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"Netlify:"},{"s":" a Log Drain (Netlify Enterprise), set up the same way."}],[{"b":"Cloudflare in front of your site:"},{"s":" pages Cloudflare serves from its cache never reach your server. Cloudflare's own request log (Logpush) or the small Skald Worker, on any plan, sends them to Skald. No visit is counted twice. See the "},{"a":"FAQ","href":"#help?part=faq"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The full list of hosts, with what each one lets Skald see: "},{"a":"Hosting","href":"https://github.com/spcaeo/skald/blob/main/docs/HOSTING.md"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"How fresh the figures are"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The foot of every page says when the data was last updated, and when the next update is due. Today's figures are recounted about every two minutes. Yesterday becomes a whole day after the morning's daily run."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If your server allows it, "},{"b":"Refresh"},{"s":" in the top bar recounts today at once."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Next steps"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"a":"Sign-in and team","href":"#help?part=sign-in-and-team"}],[{"a":"Internal traffic","href":"#help?part=internal-traffic"},{"s":": keep your own visits out of the figures."}],[{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"}],[{"a":"FAQ","href":"#help?part=faq"}]]}]},{"id":"docker-first-install","title":"Docker: first install in 10 minutes","summary":[{"s":"From nothing to a working dashboard on a server that already runs your website with nginx: run the container, sign in, fill the last 14 days, check it with the doctor, then add the script tag and hooks."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"1. Run it (2 minutes)"},{"t":"pre","text":"docker run -d --name skald --restart unless-stopped \\\n  -p 127.0.0.1:8080:8080 \\\n  -v /var/log/nginx:/logs:ro \\\n  -v skald-data:/var/lib/skald \\\n  -e SKALD_SITE=example.com \\\n  -e SKALD_HOSTS=\"example.com www.example.com\" \\\n  -e SKALD_TIMEZONE=America/New_York \\\n  -e SKALD_BASE_URL=https://www.example.com \\\n  -e SKALD_TRUSTED_PROXIES=private -e SKALD_REAL_IP_HEADER=X-Real-IP \\\n  ghcr.io/spcaeo/skald:2"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"code":"127.0.0.1:"},{"s":" publishes the port on this machine only. nginx in front gives it to the world. Keep the same line in every later "},{"code":"docker run"},{"s":"."}],[{"code":"/var/log/nginx"},{"s":" is read-only: Skald reads the log, never changes it."}],[{"code":"skald-data"},{"s":" holds everything Skald keeps. It must be mounted at "},{"code":"/var/lib/skald"},{"s":", where the image keeps its data. Keep the volume."}],[{"code":":2"},{"s":" follows every 2.x release and never a breaking one."}],[{"s":"Not a Next.js site? Add "},{"code":"-e SKALD_ASSET_PREFIXES=\"/wp-content/ /wp-includes/\""},{"s":" (WordPress), or the folder your pages load their scripts and styles from. A visit counts as people only when its browser fetched one."}],[{"s":"The last line is for nginx on the same machine. It lets Skald see each visitor's address, not nginx's."}],[{"s":"Countries: nginx's stock log has no country. To get one, give Skald a GeoIP country file. DB-IP's free country file works. Keep it on the host, for example in "},{"code":"/usr/share/GeoIP"},{"s":", and add "},{"code":"-v /usr/share/GeoIP:/geoip:ro -e SKALD_COUNTRY_DB=/geoip/dbip-country-lite.mmdb"},{"s":". Each visit then gets its address's country, and so does a lead your backend sends with an address. Refresh the file on the host once a month (your updater or a cron job that downloads DB-IP's new file). Skald reads the new file by itself, no restart. DB-IP's credit is shown under the countries. Without a file, countries say Unknown. A country your log already carries (Cloudflare's, or nginx's own "},{"code":"cc="},{"s":") always wins."}],[{"s":"A new install keeps each visit with its IP address, and each lead's name and email, so admins can look a person up. To keep neither, add "},{"code":"-e SKALD_KEEP_IPS=0 -e SKALD_IDENTITY=anonymous"},{"s":". Admins can change both later in "},{"b":"Settings > Data retention > People"},{"s":". See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"2. Put it on the web (2 minutes)"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"In your site's HTTPS "},{"code":"server { }"},{"s":" block, before "},{"code":"location /"},{"s":":"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"location ^~ /traffic {\n    access_log off;\n    proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8080;\n    proxy_set_header Host $host;\n    proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\n    proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\n    client_max_body_size 6m;\n}"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Then check and reload. Careful: your website shares this nginx, so never reload without the check."}]},{"t":"pre","text":"sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx"},{"t":"h2","text":"3. Sign in (1 minute)"},{"t":"pre","text":"docker exec -it skald skald accounts init --org \"Example Co\" --owner-email owner@example.com"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"It prints a \"set your password\" link, valid 60 minutes. Open it, set a password, and you are in at "},{"code":"https://www.example.com/traffic/"},{"s":". See "},{"a":"Sign-in and team","href":"#help?part=sign-in-and-team"},{"s":" to invite others."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"4. Fill the last 14 days (2 minutes)"},{"t":"pre","text":"docker exec skald skald backfill --days 14"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"It stores each day the log's rotations still hold. Today fills by itself within two minutes."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"5. Ask the doctor (1 minute)"},{"t":"pre","text":"docker exec skald skald doctor"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"One line per part, each OK, NEEDS ATTENTION or OFF, and the fix in plain words:"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Line"}],[{"s":"Checks"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Daily run"}],[{"s":"It ran in the last day, and did not fail"}]],[[{"s":"Days stored"}],[{"s":"None of the last 14 days is missing or withheld; if some are, the backfill command"}]],[[{"s":"Access log"}],[{"s":"The log is there, readable, and written today"}]],[[{"s":"Page assets"}],[{"s":"A browser fetched your page assets: without them nobody counts as a person"}]],[[{"s":"Web app"}],[{"s":"The dashboard has its menu"}]],[[{"s":"Hook receiver"}],[{"s":"The part that takes hooks and the script tag answers"}]],[[{"s":"Hook ..."}],[{"s":"Each hook: its secret, and its last delivery"}]],[[{"s":"One lead, two tools"}],[{"s":"The same lead arrived through two tools (two hooks, or a hook and the lead database), so it counts twice"}]],[[{"s":"Script tag"}],[{"s":"Its origins, and the last event from a page"}]],[[{"s":"Lead database"}],[{"s":"The website's lead database can be read, when one is set"}]],[[{"s":"Mail"}],[{"s":"The mail settings are complete"}]],[[{"s":"Version"}],[{"s":"A newer release, from the last daily check (it never goes online itself)"}]],[[{"s":"Disk"}],[{"s":"Free space where Skald keeps its data"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"OFF is a part you have not turned on. It exits 1 when anything needs attention, so a script can watch it. "},{"code":"--json"},{"s":" prints the same list as JSON. "},{"code":"--send-test"},{"s":" also sends one test mail to the recipients."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The daily run happens at 07:15 in the site's time zone. Before the first one, \"Daily run: has never run here\" is expected."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"6. Add the script tag (2 minutes)"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The tag gives form steps, clicks and booking widgets. Start the container again with your site's origin:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"docker rm -f skald\ndocker run ... -e SKALD_BEACON_ORIGINS=https://www.example.com ...    # the same command, plus this line"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Then copy the tag from "},{"b":"Settings > Integrations"},{"s":" into every page's head. See "},{"a":"Tracking script","href":"#help?part=tracking-script"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Only the first site needs "},{"code":"SKALD_BEACON_ORIGINS"},{"s":". A site you add later from the dashboard takes events from its own "},{"b":"Host names"},{"s":" ("},{"b":"Settings > This site > Sites"},{"s":"). Its page assets are its own too: a site that is not Next.js sets them in "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Sites > Page assets"},{"s":" ("},{"code":"SKALD_ASSET_PREFIXES"},{"s":" is for the first site only). See "},{"a":"Tracking script","href":"#help?part=tracking-script"},{"s":", \"More than one site\"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"7. Add hooks"},{"t":"p","in":[{"b":"Settings > Integrations > Make secret"},{"s":" for each tool, or on the server:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"docker exec skald skald hooks secret example.com lead"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Then: "},{"a":"Send leads from your backend","href":"#help?part=leads-from-your-backend"},{"s":", "},{"a":"Demo bookings","href":"#help?part=demo-bookings"},{"s":", and "},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":" for the other tools. Not sure which? "},{"a":"Pick your road","href":"#help?part=pick-your-road"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Upgrade"},{"t":"pre","text":"docker pull ghcr.io/spcaeo/skald:2\ndocker rm -f skald\ndocker run ...        # the same command as before"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The volume keeps all data. Not during the daily run."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"When something is wrong"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"You see"}],[{"s":"Why"}],[{"s":"Fix"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"A plain page with no menu"}],[{"s":"An old image"}],[{"s":"Pull the new image; the doctor's "},{"b":"Web app"},{"s":" line says so"}]],[[{"s":"\"nothing parsed\""}],[{"s":"The log is not mounted, or not readable"}],[{"code":"docker exec skald ls -l /logs"},{"s":"; the container's user is in group "},{"code":"adm"},{"s":" (gid 4), which reads "},{"code":"/var/log/nginx"},{"s":" on Ubuntu and Debian"}]],[[{"s":"No person counted"}],[{"s":"No page asset seen"}],[{"s":"Set "},{"code":"SKALD_ASSET_PREFIXES"},{"s":" (the first site) or "},{"b":"Settings > Sites > Page assets"},{"s":" (a site added later); the doctor's "},{"b":"Page assets"},{"s":" line says which"}]],[[{"s":"A hook answers 404"}],[{"s":"The hook has no secret"}],[{"s":"Make its secret"}]],[[{"s":"A hook answers 502"}],[{"s":"An image older than 2.2.2"}],[{"s":"Pull the new image"}]],[[{"s":"\"Too many tries\" on sign-in for everyone"}],[{"s":"The proxy in front is not trusted"}],[{"s":"Set "},{"code":"SKALD_TRUSTED_PROXIES"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"SKALD_REAL_IP_HEADER"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"code":"docker logs skald"},{"s":" shows one line per job."}]}]},{"id":"pick-your-road","title":"Pick your road","summary":[{"s":"Which way your site's leads, bookings and payments should reach Skald, by the kind of site you run: what each road gives you, what it cannot see, and what to set."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"The roads"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald always reads your web server's log: visits, pages, sources, AI assistants and bots. Conversions come in by four other roads. Pick the ones that fit your site."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Road"}],[{"s":"What it is"}],[{"s":"Set up in"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"The script tag"}],[{"s":"One line in every page's head. It reports form steps, phone and email clicks, booking widgets and button clicks"}],[{"a":"Tracking script","href":"#help?part=tracking-script"}]],[[{"s":"The lead hook"}],[{"s":"Your site's own server tells Skald \"a lead was made\", in a signed message"}],[{"a":"Send leads from your backend","href":"#help?part=leads-from-your-backend"}]],[[{"s":"Tool hooks"}],[{"s":"Calendly, Cal.com, Stripe, HubSpot, Typeform, Zapier or Make send their own signed messages"}],[{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"}]],[[{"s":"The lead database"}],[{"s":"Skald reads your site's own lead store, with no change to the website"}],[{"s":"the server's config ("},{"code":"leads.db"},{"s":")"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The lead database road reads "},{"b":"SQLite only"},{"s":": a Payload-style "},{"code":"submissions"},{"s":" table. It cannot read MySQL, Postgres or a WordPress database. For those, use the lead hook."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"By kind of site"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Your site"}],[{"s":"Road"}],[{"s":"What you get"}],[{"s":"What you do not get"}],[{"s":"What to set"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"WordPress or another CMS with a form plugin"}],[{"s":"Script tag, plus the "},{"code":"json"},{"s":" hook through Zapier or Make (or the plugin's own webhook, if it can sign)"}],[{"s":"Forms started and sent, phone and email clicks, each lead with its source"}],[{"s":"The lead's later status (won, lost), unless your CRM sends it"}],[{"s":"The tag on every page; "},{"code":"data-skald=\"contact\""},{"s":" on the contact form; a Zap or scenario that posts to the "},{"code":"json"},{"s":" hook"}]],[[{"s":"Next.js on Vercel"}],[{"s":"Script tag, plus the signed "},{"code":"lead"},{"s":" hook from an API route or server action"}],[{"s":"Every lead your server makes, with its first and last touch"}],[{"s":"The visit figures, until Vercel's logs reach Skald through a log drain"}],[{"s":"The tag; the hook secret in Vercel's environment variables; a log drain ("},{"code":"docs/CDN-LOGS.md"},{"s":")"}]],[[{"s":"A site with a Postgres or MySQL backend"}],[{"s":"The signed "},{"code":"lead"},{"s":" hook from the backend"}],[{"s":"Every lead, on the server's word, even when a browser blocks scripts"}],[{"s":"Form steps, unless you add the script tag too"}],[{"s":"The hook secret in the backend's environment"}]],[[{"s":"A site that keeps leads in SQLite (Payload CMS)"}],[{"s":"The lead database"}],[{"s":"Every lead, its status (won, lost, spam) and its touches, with no code"}],[{"s":"Leads from other places"}],[{"code":"leads.db"},{"s":" in the server's config"}]],[[{"s":"No-code site (Webflow, Squarespace, Wix)"}],[{"s":"Script tag, plus Zapier or Make to the "},{"code":"json"},{"s":" hook"}],[{"s":"Form steps and clicks from the tag; the form's leads from Zapier or Make"}],[{"s":"Anything the builder will not let you add to the page head"}],[{"s":"The tag in the site's custom code; a Zap that posts to the "},{"code":"json"},{"s":" hook"}]],[[{"s":"Calendly or Cal.com"}],[{"s":"The tool's hook, plus the embed through the script tag"}],[{"s":"Bookings, cancellations, reschedules and no-shows; opened and time chosen when embedded"}],[{"s":"Opened and time chosen when you only link to the booking page"}],[{"s":"See "},{"a":"Demo bookings","href":"#help?part=demo-bookings"}]],[[{"s":"Stripe"}],[{"s":"The "},{"code":"stripe"},{"s":" hook"}],[{"s":"Each paid checkout, and one paid later by a slow method"}],[{"s":"Refunds, subscriptions, customer details (never read)"}],[{"s":"The endpoint's signing secret ("},{"code":"whsec_..."},{"s":"), pasted on the Integrations page; the visitor ID as the session's "},{"code":"client_reference_id"}]],[[{"s":"HubSpot"}],[{"s":"The "},{"code":"hubspot"},{"s":" hook, or Zapier to the "},{"code":"json"},{"s":" hook"}],[{"s":"New contacts, booked meetings, deals won"}],[{"s":"Anything HubSpot does not send"}],[{"s":"The app's client secret, pasted on the Integrations page"}]],[[{"s":"Zapier, Make, n8n"}],[{"s":"The "},{"code":"json"},{"s":" hook"}],[{"s":"Any lead any tool knows about, up to 100 in one message"}],[{"s":"Nothing by itself: it sends what the Zap sends"}],[{"b":"Make secret"},{"s":" for "},{"code":"json"},{"s":", and the signing step in the Zap"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Never sign a hook in the browser. The secret must stay on a server. A browser can only use the script tag."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What each road costs in privacy"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Visitor IDs are off by default."},{"s":" Then the script tag makes no ID, and a hook's "},{"code":"vid"},{"s":" is dropped before anything is kept. Journeys, abandoned forms and assisted sources need the IDs on. Your privacy notice must say so."}],[{"b":"Names and emails are kept only when Leads' names and emails is full"},{"s":" ("},{"b":"Settings > Data retention > People"},{"s":"). That is the default for a new install; an install upgraded from before 2.4.0 keeps none until an admin turns it on. Then the name and the primary email only. Nothing else, ever: no phone, no address, no message."}],[{"b":"Addresses and browsers."},{"s":" A lead hook may send the visitor's address and browser once. Skald looks up the country and the device, then drops both."}],[{"b":"The log itself."},{"s":" With "},{"b":"Keep visitors' IP addresses"},{"s":" on (also the default for a new install), each visit in the log is kept with its address, so admins can look a person up. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"The lead database"},{"s":" is opened read-only. Only the columns Skald needs are read."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"One lead, one road"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Send each lead through one road only. Each tool keeps its own row, so the same lead sent through two (for example the lead hook and Zapier, or the lead hook and the lead database) counts twice."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"b":"Settings > Integrations > Status"},{"s":" flags it: \"One lead, two tools\", with the leads it saw. Turn one of the two roads off for those leads."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Check it"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"On the server: "},{"code":"sudo skald doctor"},{"s":" (Docker: "},{"code":"docker exec skald skald doctor"},{"s":"). It lists every part with OK or NEEDS ATTENTION, and the fix."}],[{"s":"In the dashboard: "},{"b":"Settings > Integrations > Status"},{"s":" shows the same lines for the roads in, and each hook says \"ready\", \"never received\" or \"last received 2 h ago\"."}]]}]},{"id":"sign-in-and-team","title":"Sign-in and team","summary":[{"s":"How to sign in, keep your account safe with two-step sign-in, and invite your team with the right role."}],"blocks":[{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"These pages come with accounts. If your server uses one shared login instead, its users are listed under "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > Users"},{"s":", and the server admin manages them."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Sign in"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open your dashboard's address. The sign-in page opens."}],[{"s":"Type your "},{"b":"Email"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"Password"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Sign in"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Every password field has a "},{"b":"Show"},{"s":" button at its right edge. Select it to see what you typed, and "},{"b":"Hide"},{"s":" to cover it again. The password is always covered again before the form is sent."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Keep me signed in"},{"t":"p","in":[{"b":"Keep me signed in"},{"s":" is ticked by default. You then stay signed in for 14 days on that device, counted from your last use. Untick it on a shared computer: you are signed out when the browser closes."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Your organisation can set a shorter session length. See "},{"a":"Settings and retention","href":"#help?part=settings-and-retention"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Too many tries"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"After 5 failed tries for one email address in 15 minutes, each new try waits 30 seconds. You are never locked out for good, so nobody can lock you out by guessing."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Forgot your password"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"On the sign-in page, select "},{"b":"Forgot password?"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Type the email address you sign in with."}],[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Send the link"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Open the mail and follow the link. It works once, for 60 minutes."}],[{"s":"Type a "},{"b":"New password"},{"s":" twice and select "},{"b":"Save the new password"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The page says the same words whether or not the address has an account. No mail after a few minutes? Check the spam folder, or ask an admin of your team."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Saving a new password signs out every other session of your account."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"If your server cannot send mail, ask the person who runs the server. They can make a reset link for you."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Password rules"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"At least 12 characters."}],[{"s":"Not your email address."}],[{"s":"Not a common password."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Two-step sign-in"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Two-step sign-in asks for a 6-digit code from an app on your phone, after your password. Any authenticator app works."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Turn it on"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Go to "},{"b":"Settings > You > Your account"},{"s":", or open "},{"a":"Your account","href":"#settings/account"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Two-step sign-in"},{"s":", type your password and select "},{"b":"Turn on two-step sign-in"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"In your authenticator app, add an account and type the key the page shows. If your app takes an address instead, use the address shown."}],[{"s":"Type the 6-digit code the app shows, then select "},{"b":"Confirm"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"The page shows 10 recovery codes. Select "},{"b":"Copy all"},{"s":" or "},{"b":"Download as text"},{"s":" and keep them somewhere safe."}],[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"I have saved them"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The recovery codes are shown only this once. Each one lets you sign in once if you lose your phone."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Sign in with two-step sign-in"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Type your email and password as usual."}],[{"s":"In "},{"b":"Code"},{"s":", type the 6 digits your app shows now, or one of your recovery codes."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Codes change every 30 seconds. If a code is refused, try the one the app shows now."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Turn it off"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Go to "},{"a":"Your account","href":"#settings/account"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Two-step sign-in"},{"s":", type your password and select "},{"b":"Turn off"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If your organisation requires two-step sign-in, the sign-in page asks you to set it up the next time you sign in."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Lost your phone and your recovery codes? Ask the person who runs the server to turn two-step sign-in off for you."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Your account"},{"t":"p","in":[{"b":"Settings > You > Your account"},{"s":" changes only your own account. Everyone has this page, viewers too."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"You"},{"s":": your name, and the address and role you are signed in with. Select "},{"b":"Save name"},{"s":" after a change."}],[{"b":"Password"},{"s":": type your current password and the new one twice, then select "},{"b":"Change password"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"Two-step sign-in"},{"s":": turn it on or off."}],[{"b":"Where you are signed in"},{"s":": each browser, when it signed in and when it was last seen."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To end every other session, select "},{"b":"Sign out everywhere else"},{"s":", then "},{"b":"Yes, sign them out"},{"s":". Use this if you signed in on a computer you no longer use."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Roles"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A person has one role in each organisation."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Role"}],[{"s":"May"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Viewer"}],[{"s":"See every page of the organisation's sites and the team list. Change their own name, password and two-step sign-in. Changes nothing else. Cannot look a person up, and sees the left-out lists without names, emails or visitor IDs"}]],[[{"s":"Admin"}],[{"s":"All of that, plus: invite, remove and change members (not owners), make API tokens, read the audit log, change the site's settings, and look a person up (the search at the top: visits with their IP address, emails, names)"}]],[[{"s":"Owner"}],[{"s":"All of that, plus: make, change or remove owners, set the security rules, remove a site, and handle billing"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"An organisation always keeps at least one owner."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Some settings apply to every site on the server, not only yours: the AI crawler rules, saved funnels, the internal-address list, the mail server and the log file paths. Only an "},{"b":"install admin"},{"s":" may change those. This is a flag the server admin gives to a person."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Invite people"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"You must be an admin or owner."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Go to "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > Team"},{"s":", or open "},{"a":"Team","href":"#settings/team"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Invite someone"},{"s":", type the person's "},{"b":"Email"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Pick a "},{"b":"Role"},{"s":". Only an owner can invite another owner."}],[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Send invite"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The person gets a mail with a link. It works once, for 7 days. On the invite page they pick a name and a password and select "},{"b":"Create account and join"},{"s":". If they already have an account with that address, the button reads "},{"b":"Join"},{"s":" and the organisation's name. They keep their own password and sign in with it."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If mail is not set up on your server, the page says \"Mail is not set up; send this link yourself.\" Copy the link and send it to the person yourself. They then choose a new password at their first sign-in, so you never know the password they go on to use."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Pending invites"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open invites are listed under "},{"b":"Pending invites"},{"s":", with who sent them and when they expire."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Resend"},{"s":" sends a new link and replaces the old one."}],[{"b":"Cancel"},{"s":" stops the link at once."}]]},{"t":"h3","text":"Change a role or remove someone"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Members"},{"s":", each person's email, name, role, last seen and two-step sign-in are listed."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"To change a role, pick a new one in the "},{"b":"Role"},{"s":" list. It saves at once."}],[{"s":"To remove someone, select "},{"b":"Remove"},{"s":", then "},{"b":"Yes, remove"},{"s":". Their sessions for this organisation end at once."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"You cannot change your own role or remove yourself. Viewers see the team list with every control turned off."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Sign out"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Select the round "},{"b":"You"},{"s":" button at the foot of the sidebar, then "},{"b":"Sign out"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Or, on "},{"a":"Your account","href":"#settings/account"},{"s":", select "},{"b":"Sign out of this browser"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Related guides"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"a":"Getting started","href":"#help?part=getting-started"}],[{"a":"Settings and retention","href":"#help?part=settings-and-retention"}],[{"a":"API","href":"#help?part=api"},{"s":": tokens for scripts."}]]}]},{"id":"internal-traffic","title":"Internal traffic: leave your own visits out","summary":[{"s":"Tell Skald which internet addresses belong to you and your team, so your own visits do not count as visitors. This guide covers adding your address, adding a range by hand, removing one, and what changes in the figures."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"Why your own visits should not count"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"You and your team open the site all day: to check a page, test a form, or show a client. If those visits counted, your figures would look busier than they are. A new page would seem popular because you opened it ten times."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald keeps these visits apart. They are not deleted. They go into their own group, "},{"b":"our own traffic"},{"s":", so the five groups still add up to everything in the server log. They are never counted as visitors or people."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Where to find it"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Internal traffic"},{"s":", or go straight to "},{"a":"Internal traffic","href":"#settings/internal"},{"s":". Settings opens from the gear at the foot of the sidebar."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The page is headed "},{"b":"Our own traffic"},{"s":". The list of addresses is in the section "},{"b":"Internal addresses"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Add your own address"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"This is the quickest way. Do it once from each place you work: the office, home, a laptop on another network."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Internal traffic"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Internal addresses"},{"s":", type a label in the box beside "},{"b":"Add my current address"},{"s":", for example \"Office Mac\" or \"Home\"."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Add my current address"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Check that the new line shows in the list."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald adds the internet address your browser is using right now. You do not need to know it or type it."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Many home connections get a new address from time to time. If your visits start to show up as visitors again, add your current address again, or ask your internet provider for your range and add the range instead."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"On a VPN, the address added is the VPN's. Your visits count as yours only while you use that same VPN."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Add an address or range by hand"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Use this for a teammate who is not on your network, a test machine, or a whole office range."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Internal traffic"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"In "},{"b":"Address or range"},{"s":", type one address, such as "},{"code":"192.0.2.10"},{"s":", or a range, such as "},{"code":"198.51.100.0/24"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"In "},{"b":"Label"},{"s":", type whose it is, for example \"Berlin office\"."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Add address"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Both the address and the label are needed. A label can be up to 60 characters."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"What you can enter:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"one IPv4 address, such as "},{"code":"203.0.113.5"},{"s":";"}],[{"s":"one IPv6 address;"}],[{"s":"a range written with a slash, such as "},{"code":"198.51.100.0/24"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A range may be at most "},{"code":"/16"},{"s":" wide for IPv4 and "},{"code":"/32"},{"s":" for IPv6. Wider ranges are refused, because they would hide real visitors."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Ask your IT team or internet provider for your office range. Do not guess: a range that is too wide hides real visitors from you."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Remove an address"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Internal traffic"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Find the line in the list and press "},{"b":"Remove"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Yes, remove"},{"s":", or "},{"b":"Keep it"},{"s":" to change your mind."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"From then on, visits from that address count as an ordinary visitor's again."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"The list"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each line shows the "},{"b":"Address or range"},{"s":", its "},{"b":"Label"},{"s":", and "},{"b":"Since"},{"s":": the day it was added."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"The list holds at most 50 entries. When it is full, remove one before you add another."}],[{"s":"Some lines show a lock and the word "},{"b":"locked"},{"s":". They were set on the server, in its config file, and can only be changed there. Ask whoever runs your server."}],[{"s":"The list applies to every site on your Skald server, not only the one you are looking at."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"What changes in the figures, and from when"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"An address counts as yours "},{"b":"from the moment you add it"},{"s":". Nothing is recounted backwards."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"From now on:"},{"s":" visits from the address go to "},{"b":"our own traffic"},{"s":", in the live view and in every day collected after that moment."}],[{"b":"Earlier today:"},{"s":" visits from before you pressed the button stay where they were counted."}],[{"b":"Past days:"},{"s":" they stay exactly as they were. A past visit from a newly added address stays a visitor."}],[{"b":"After you remove it:"},{"s":" visits from the address count as visitors again from that moment. Past days keep what they had."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"This is on purpose. A day's figures never change after they are stored, so a report you sent last month still matches the dashboard today."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Add your addresses on your first day with Skald, before you start testing the site. That keeps your early figures clean."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Our machines and the heartbeat"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The same page shows everything Skald counts as your own traffic, not only the addresses in the list:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Our own requests"},{"s":": every request from your own machines and tools together."}],[{"b":"By machine or tool"},{"s":": each one by its label, such as the office, your own crawler, browser tests, or the heartbeat. Labels for tools are set on the server."}],[{"b":"How fast the server answered"},{"s":": server time per hour for the last whole day."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Uptime from the heartbeat, and every outage, is on "},{"a":"Site > Health","href":"#site/health"},{"s":", under "},{"b":"Is the site up?"},{"s":":"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Uptime, from the heartbeat"},{"s":": the heartbeat is one request every five minutes to your site. If it is answered, the site is up. A red day had a gap of more than 10 minutes or a failed answer: the site was down, or the heartbeat itself stopped."}],[{"b":"Outages and heartbeat gaps"},{"s":": each gap, with when it started, when it ended, and how many minutes it lasted."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"You see the heartbeat parts only if your server runs a heartbeat."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Who may change the list"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"It depends on how people sign in to your server."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Server type"}],[{"s":"Who may add or remove"}],[{"s":"Who may see the list"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Team accounts"}],[{"s":"An install admin only, because the list applies to every site on the server"}],[{"s":"Install admins see every entry. Other admins see the entries added on their own sites, but cannot change them"}]],[[{"s":"One shared login"}],[{"s":"Admins"}],[{"s":"Everyone who signs in; viewers cannot change it"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"On a server with team accounts, a viewer does not see the addresses at all. The page says the list is for admins, because it holds the addresses of the people who work on the site."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If the buttons are greyed out, hover over one to see why. Ask an install admin to add your address for you. See "},{"a":"Sign-in and team","href":"#help?part=sign-in-and-team"},{"s":" for roles."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Privacy"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Your team's list of addresses is shown only on this page and kept in the server's change log. Like every visitor's address, your team's requests also show, behind sign-in, in the last 6 hours of "},{"a":"Site > Requests","href":"#site/requests"},{"s":". The list itself never appears in the data files, CSV downloads, the API or mail. Every add and remove is logged with who did it and when."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":" for more."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"If something goes wrong"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Message"}],[{"s":"What it means"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"\"Give it a label first\""}],[{"s":"Type a label before you press "},{"b":"Add my current address"}]],[[{"s":"\"Both an address (or range) and a label are needed\""}],[{"s":"Fill in both boxes"}]],[[{"s":"\"is not an IP address or range\""}],[{"s":"Check the address for typing mistakes"}]],[[{"s":"\"that range is too wide\""}],[{"s":"Use a narrower range: at most "},{"code":"/16"},{"s":" for IPv4, "},{"code":"/32"},{"s":" for IPv6"}]],[[{"s":"\"is already listed\""}],[{"s":"The address is in the list already, perhaps as a locked line"}]],[[{"s":"\"The list is full\""}],[{"s":"Remove an entry first; the list holds 50"}]],[[{"s":"\"your address is not known here\""}],[{"s":"The server cannot see your address. Add it by hand instead"}]],[[{"s":"\"Only an install admin can change this\""}],[{"s":"Ask an install admin"}]]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Related guides"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"a":"Getting started","href":"#help?part=getting-started"},{"s":": the first things to set up."}],[{"a":"Settings and retention","href":"#help?part=settings-and-retention"},{"s":": the other settings pages."}],[{"a":"FAQ","href":"#help?part=faq"},{"s":": common questions about the figures."}]]}]},{"id":"leads-and-conversions","title":"Leads and conversions","summary":[{"s":"Where Skald's leads and conversions come from, what the "},{"b":"Leads & sales"},{"s":" section shows, what \"abandoned\" means, and how to see every lead and conversion the figures leave out. The tabs show counts; a person's own leads, emails and visits are in the person search (owners and admins)."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"Leads & sales: five tabs, one options row"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Everything about results sits in "},{"b":"Leads & sales"},{"s":" in the menu:"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Tab"}],[{"s":"What it answers"}]],"rows":[[[{"a":"Pipeline","href":"#sales/pipeline"}],[{"s":"How many leads, at which stage, from where, how fast"}]],[[{"a":"Bookings","href":"#sales/bookings"}],[{"s":"Demo bookings and payments from your booking and payment tools: opened, chose a time, booked, cancelled, rescheduled, no-show, won"}]],[[{"a":"Funnels","href":"#sales/funnels"}],[{"s":"Any series of pages and events. See "},{"a":"Funnels and goals","href":"#help?part=funnels-and-goals"}]],[[{"a":"Events","href":"#sales/events"}],[{"s":"What readers did inside your pages, from the script tag"}]],[[{"a":"People","href":"#sales/people"}],[{"s":"Find one person, and the people who converted lately"}]]]},{"t":"h3","text":"Count from: two roads, never added"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Pipeline has one row of options above its figures. The first one, "},{"b":"Count from"},{"s":", picks where the figures come from:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Lead database"},{"s":" (the default) counts the leads in your website's own lead database: sign-ups, contact forms, early-access requests and demo bookings, as your team marks them."}],[{"b":"Tools"},{"s":" counts every action that matters, from every road at once: your booking, form and payment tools, the script tag on your pages, and the lead database."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The two are never added together, and never share a table. A booking that reaches Skald from Calendly, or a form from Typeform, shows only with "},{"b":"Tools"},{"s":". A line under the options says which road the figures come from."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The other options narrow what you see:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Source"},{"s":": one source (lead database only; the tools do not split their stages by source, so it is greyed with the reason)."}],[{"b":"Action"},{"s":": one kind of lead or action, for example Demo booking or Sign-up."}],[{"b":"Stage"},{"s":": one status: New, Contacted, Qualified, Won or Lost (lead database only)."}],[{"b":"Show left out"},{"s":": list what the figures leave out, right under the options. With the lead database: Spam, Duplicates, Test. With the tools: Cancelled or no-show, Removed, Test. These are lists, never added to a figure."}],[{"b":"Period"},{"s":": the same period as the top bar's. Changing one changes both."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The address keeps every option, so a link or a reload opens the same view. An older "},{"code":"#leads"},{"s":" link opens Pipeline counting from the lead database, and "},{"code":"#conversions"},{"s":" opens it counting from the tools, so each shows the figures it showed before."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Leads on every page"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Leads and demo bookings also show where you look at your visitors, so you can see which source, page or country brings them. All of these use the tools' figures (Count from: Tools), from every road at once."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A "},{"b":"lead"},{"s":" here is a form sent (contact, sign-up, early access, trial) or a demo booked, once completed. "},{"b":"Demos booked"},{"s":" are counted on their own as well. Payments, deals and clicks are not leads. A conversion marked test is never counted."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Tab"}],[{"s":"What you see"}]],"rows":[[[{"a":"Overview > Summary","href":"#overview/summary"}],[{"b":"Leads"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"Demos booked"},{"s":" tiles for the period, with the change against the period before. Pink dots on the main chart: each day's leads."}]],[[{"s":"Overview > Summary, with "},{"b":"Today · Live"},{"s":" on"}],[{"s":"The "},{"b":"Leads"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"Demos booked"},{"s":" tiles for today so far, and "},{"b":"Leads and bookings today"},{"s":", the 5 newest: time, what it was (contact form, demo booking, sign-up), its stage, source, landing page and country with its flag. A link opens all of today's on Pipeline. A started form is listed with its stage, and is not a lead. Test rows are listed and marked \"test, not counted\"."}]],[[{"a":"Traffic > Sources","href":"#traffic/sources"}],[{"b":"Leads"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"Lead rate"},{"s":" beside each source's visitors."}]],[[{"a":"Traffic > Pages","href":"#traffic/pages"}],[{"b":"Landing pages, with leads"},{"s":": visitors who started on each page, its leads and lead rate."}]],[[{"a":"Traffic > Places & devices","href":"#traffic/places"}],[{"b":"Leads"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"Lead rate"},{"s":" beside each country."}]],[[{"a":"Overview > Insights","href":"#overview/insights"}],[{"s":"Findings about leads, for example \"Leads from AI assistant up 60% week on week\" or \"/pricing/ is the page that started the most leads\"."}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"With "},{"b":"Compare with…"},{"s":" on, the Traffic grids add the other period's visitors and the change; their lead columns stay the period in the top bar's."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Which touch each column uses:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Sources"},{"s":": the last touch, the source of the visit the lead was sent from."}],[{"b":"Pages"},{"s":": the landing page recorded with the lead (its first visit's, when known)."}],[{"b":"Places & devices"},{"s":": the lead's country, from the tool or the visitor's address."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The honesty rules are the same as everywhere:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Only days with "},{"b":"checked"},{"s":" conversions count. A day the second count disagreed on is withheld. A day before conversions were recorded is \"not recorded\", never zero."}],[{"s":"The "},{"b":"lead rate"},{"s":" is leads per visitor over the same days only: days whole in the visitor figures "},{"i":"and"},{"s":" checked in conversions. It is given over at least 10 visitors. Below that you see the count alone, with \"too few to say\"."}],[{"s":"A "},{"b":"change"},{"s":" (Overview, Compare with…) is shown only when both periods are whole and every day of both has checked conversions."}],[{"b":"Insights"},{"s":" about leads follow the same rules as the others: two whole periods, at least 5 leads, a change of at least 20%. A finding the second count does not confirm is left out, and the tab says so."}],[{"s":"Leads are counted for the whole site. On a page group (for example one language), the lead columns are not shown."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"A lead reported by two roads (for example the script tag and the lead database, for the same form) counts on each, as on Pipeline with Count from: Tools. A lead that arrived from two tools with the same reference (for example the lead hook and Zapier, or a hook and the lead database) is flagged as \"One lead, two tools\" under "},{"b":"Settings > Integrations > Status"},{"s":" and by the server's doctor command. The script tag's own rows are not part of that check."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Where leads and conversions come from"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"There are four sources. You can use one or all of them."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Source"}],[{"s":"What it gives"}],[{"s":"Shown on"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Your website's lead database"}],[{"s":"every lead, its kind, its status, first and last touch"}],[{"s":"Pipeline (Lead database and Tools)"}]],[[{"s":"Your site's lead push (the "},{"code":"lead"},{"s":" hook)"}],[{"s":"a lead your own server reports the moment it is made"}],[{"s":"Pipeline (Tools)"}]],[[{"s":"Webhooks from your tools"}],[{"s":"bookings, cancellations, no-shows, form answers, payments, CRM deals"}],[{"s":"Pipeline (Tools) and Bookings"}]],[[{"s":"The "},{"code":"skald.js"},{"s":" script tag"}],[{"s":"forms started and sent, booking widgets opened and booked, phone and email clicks"}],[{"s":"Pipeline (Tools), Bookings and Events"}]]]},{"t":"h3","text":"The lead database"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If your website keeps its leads in its own database, the person who runs your Skald server can point Skald at it. Skald opens it read-only and never changes it. Every two minutes it reads the leads that changed."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Leads marked "},{"code":"spam"},{"s":" or "},{"code":"duplicate"},{"s":" are left out of every count, and counted apart. They are listed in full on Pipeline: "},{"b":"Show left out"},{"s":" with the lead database."}],[{"s":"A lead's status (new, contacted, qualified, won, lost) is read as it is now. When your team changes a status, past days change with it."}],[{"s":"Names and emails are read and kept only when "},{"b":"Leads' names and emails"},{"s":" is "},{"b":"full"},{"s":" (Settings > Data retention > People). Owners and admins then see them in the person search and the left-out list. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"h3","text":"Your site's lead push"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Your site's own server can tell Skald \"a lead was made\" with a signed message. See "},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":", section \"Your own site's lead push\"."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Webhooks from your tools"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Calendly, Cal.com, HubSpot, Typeform, Stripe, Zapier and Make can send Skald a signed message for each booking, form or payment. This is how Skald learns about cancellations, no-shows and payments, which the page itself never sees. See "},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"The script tag"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"One line on every page lets Skald see what happens inside the page: a form started, a form sent, a booking widget opened and booked. Only the script tag can see a "},{"i":"start"},{"s":", so only it makes \"abandoned\" possible. See "},{"a":"The tracking script","href":"#help?part=tracking-script"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"One name per action"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Whatever reports it, an action gets one name, so the same thing is never counted under two names."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Action on the page"}],[{"s":"Means"}],[{"s":"Reported by"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Demos"}],[{"s":"a demo or meeting booked"}],[{"s":"Calendly, Cal.com, HubSpot meetings, the script tag, the lead database"}]],[[{"s":"Contact forms"}],[{"s":"a form sent"}],[{"s":"the script tag, Typeform, HubSpot contacts, the lead database"}]],[[{"s":"Sign-ups"}],[{"s":"a sign-up form sent"}],[{"s":"the script tag, the lead database"}]],[[{"s":"Early access"}],[{"s":"an early-access or waitlist form sent"}],[{"s":"the script tag, the lead database"}]],[[{"s":"Payments"}],[{"s":"a Stripe Checkout paid"}],[{"s":"Stripe"}]],[[{"s":"Deals"}],[{"s":"a HubSpot deal moved to won"}],[{"s":"HubSpot"}]],[[{"s":"Phone clicks, Email clicks, Button clicks"}],[{"s":"a "},{"code":"tel:"},{"s":" link, a "},{"code":"mailto:"},{"s":" link or a marked button clicked"}],[{"s":"the script tag"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each action has a "},{"i":"stage"},{"s":": started, completed, paid, cancelled, rescheduled, no-show, won or lost."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Pipeline, counting from the lead database"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Pipeline","href":"#sales/pipeline"},{"s":". "},{"b":"Count from: Lead database"},{"s":" is the default. The period governs most of the tab."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"The figures at the top"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Leads"},{"s":": sign-ups, contact forms and early access, with spam and duplicates removed."}],[{"s":"One figure per kind: Sign-ups, Contact forms, Early access, Demo opened, Demos booked."}],[{"b":"Leads per 100 visitors"},{"s":": leads against the visitors of the same verified days. It is given only over at least 10 visitors."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Under them, a line says how many spam and duplicate leads were left out. Select "},{"b":"Show them, with test leads"},{"s":", or turn on "},{"b":"Show left out"},{"s":" in the options, to see each one: when it came, its kind, page, first and last source, and its status. Leads marked test are listed there too. Owners and admins also see the email and name, when your site keeps them."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Per day, by kind"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A chart of each kind of lead per day. A hatched stub is a day with no lead counts. That day is "},{"i":"not recorded"},{"s":", never zero."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Where they came from"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each lead is shown twice, by its "},{"b":"First touch"},{"s":" and by its "},{"b":"Last touch"},{"s":":"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"First touch"},{"s":" is the source the lead's own browser remembered from its very first visit."}],[{"b":"Last touch"},{"s":" is the visit the form was sent from."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"There are four tables: by Source, by AI assistant, by Campaign and by Landing page. A lead without a value is said under the table, not shown as a row."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Likely from an AI assistant"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Many people who click a link in a ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Copilot or Gemini answer arrive with no referrer. Their touch then says \"Direct or unknown\". The "},{"b":"Likely AI (inferred)"},{"s":" table, beside the four above, gives Skald's best guess for those touches, by first touch and by last touch. It is an estimate, never a count."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"How Skald guesses:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"The touch came with no referrer and no campaign tag."}],[{"s":"When someone asks an assistant, the assistant fetches the page from your server at that moment. Skald keeps those fetches: which assistant, which page, which minute."}],[{"s":"If an assistant fetched the touch's landing page in the same minute or up to 15 minutes before, the touch is "},{"b":"likely"},{"s":" from that assistant. Your server's admin can change the window ("},{"code":"attribution.ai_window_minutes"},{"s":")."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"What it shows:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"ChatGPT"},{"s":" (or another assistant): one assistant fetched the page in the window."}],[{"b":"More than one"},{"s":": two or more did. The lead counts once."}],[{"s":"A touch that was not direct, or whose page no assistant fetched in the window, is not in the table."}],[{"b":"Not recorded"},{"s":", under the table: Skald did not keep the fetches for that time. For example, the touch is from before this feature, more than 180 days ago, or today (today's fetches are kept the next morning)."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Why only \"likely\"? A fetch can be for someone who read the answer and never clicked. A direct visit a minute later can be someone else. Skald never adds these to the AI assistant source or to any count. The (i) beside the title says the same."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Lead quality by source"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Statuses by first-touch source: New, Contacted, Qualified, Won, Lost, Spam, Duplicates. The column "},{"b":"Qualified or won, of reviewed"},{"s":" is the share of leads that are no longer new and were marked qualified or won. It is given over at least 10 reviewed leads. If every lead is still \"new\", the tab says so and shows no zeros."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Time to convert"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"From first touch to lead"},{"s":": how long after the first visit the lead came, in buckets from \"Under an hour\" to \"Over 90 days\"."}],[{"b":"Visits up to the lead"},{"s":": the browser's own count of its visits when it sent the form."}]]},{"t":"h3","text":"Funnel, by source"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"From visitors to demos booked, per source: "},{"b":"Visitors"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Saw pricing"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Opened a form"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Opened the demo"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Became a lead"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Booked a demo"},{"s":". Each step is shown as a share of that source's visitors, over at least 10 visitors."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"The first three steps are visits from your server log. The last three come from the lead database, by the lead's first-touch source. Skald puts them side by side for the same days. It never joins one lead to one visit."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Pipeline, counting from the tools"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Pipeline","href":"#sales/pipeline"},{"s":" and set "},{"b":"Count from"},{"s":" to "},{"b":"Tools"},{"s":". If nothing is set up yet, the tab lists each source as "},{"b":"On"},{"s":" or "},{"b":"Off"},{"s":" and says what to turn on."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Every action"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"One row per action, with these columns:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Started"},{"s":": starts seen by the script tag. \"not seen\" means no start was reported, for example an action only a tool reports."}],[{"b":"Completed"},{"s":": completed and paid together."}],[{"b":"Abandoned"},{"s":": see below."}],[{"b":"Completion rate"},{"s":": completed out of started, given over at least 10 starts."}],[{"b":"Cancelled or no-show"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Won"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Lost"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"h3","text":"Bookings: the demo funnel"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Leads & sales > Bookings","href":"#sales/bookings"},{"s":" holds the bookings your booking and payment tools reported (Calendly, Cal.com, Stripe), with the script tag and the lead database. Pick the booking action in "},{"b":"Booking"},{"s":". For demos: "},{"b":"Opened the booking"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Chose a time"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Booked"},{"s":", then "},{"b":"Cancelled"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Rescheduled"},{"s":", "},{"b":"No-show"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"Won"},{"s":". \"Chose a time\" is a count of page events from a Calendly embed, not of browsers. Cancelled, rescheduled and no-show need the booking tool's webhook."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Where the completed ones came from"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Completed conversions by Source (last touch), First touch, Campaign, Landing page, Country, Device and "},{"b":"Reported by"},{"s":" (which source told Skald). A value Skald was not told is shown as \"Unknown\", never guessed."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"First, last and assisted touch"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"First touch"},{"s":": where the browser, or the lead, first came from."}],[{"b":"Last touch"},{"s":": the visit it converted in."}],[{"b":"Assisted"},{"s":": a source seen earlier in a converting browser's journey that was not its last touch. Each conversion counts once per source."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Assisted needs anonymous visitor IDs (below)."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Likely from an AI assistant (conversions)"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The section "},{"b":"Likely from AI assistants (inferred)"},{"s":": completed conversions whose first touch was direct, by the assistant that likely sent them, the same guess as with the lead database. The first touch is the lead's or the tool's first touch; for the script tag, the browser's first visit. \"Not recorded\", under the table, means the first touch, or the fetches around it, were not kept. Likely, never certain, and not part of the sources above."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Time to convert"},{"t":"p","in":[{"b":"From first touch to converting"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"Visits before converting"},{"s":", for completed conversions. A conversion whose first touch is dated after it is counted as a clock error and left out."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Pages seen before converting"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"For the last 30 days: the share of converting browsers that saw each page before converting, beside the share of browsers that did not convert. Use it to ask \"does the pricing page help?\". It needs visitor IDs."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Latest conversions, on People"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Leads & sales > People","href":"#sales/people"},{"s":" lists the latest 50 completed conversions, one per browser (or per lead without one). Each shows its visits by day, the pages it read and its steps, for example \"Demo started, then completed\". No name, email or visitor ID is shown here: owners and admins find the person with "},{"b":"Find a person"},{"s":", on the same tab or at the top."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Cancelled, removed and test"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Nothing is hidden. On Pipeline (Count from: Tools), "},{"b":"Show left out"},{"s":" lists, in full, the conversions the figures do not show as completed. Bookings has the same lists under "},{"b":"Show"},{"s":":"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Cancelled or no-show"},{"s":": bookings the booking tool reported as cancelled, or as a no-show."}],[{"b":"Removed"},{"s":": rows a lead-database sync took away. For example, the lead was deleted, or marked spam. Each row is kept whole, with when and why."}],[{"b":"Test"},{"s":": conversions the server admin marked as a test. They are kept and listed, and never counted."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each one shows its row and, when it had a visitor ID, the pages it read."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Marking a conversion as a test"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A test booking or form should not count. The server admin marks it on the server:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"code":"skald conversions list example.com"},{"s":" shows the latest conversions with their numbers."}],[{"code":"skald conversions mark-test example.com 6 7"},{"s":" marks conversions 6 and 7 as test. Every stage of the same booking or lead is marked with it."}],[{"s":"To count one again: "},{"code":"skald conversions mark-test example.com 6 --unmark"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A test conversion is left out of every figure, and of the second count too. It stays listed under "},{"b":"Test"},{"s":" in "},{"b":"Show left out"},{"s":" on Pipeline, with either Count from. Each change is written to the audit log."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"For a lead in your website's lead database, mark it spam there, or give it the status "},{"code":"test"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What \"abandoned\" means"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A conversion is "},{"b":"abandoned"},{"s":" when all of this is true:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"The script tag saw it start (a form field used, a booking widget opened)."}],[{"s":"The start carried an anonymous visitor ID."}],[{"s":"Neither the same browser nor the same person (the same email, when your site sends it) completed or paid for the same action within the abandon window. The window is 24 hours unless your server sets another. So a demo opened today and booked tomorrow from another device is a booking, not an abandoned demo."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"So:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"A start still inside the window is not counted as abandoned yet."}],[{"s":"A start without a visitor ID cannot be judged, and is never counted as abandoned."}],[{"s":"Abandoned is worked out each time the tab is drawn. It is not stored."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"How a conversion is tied to a visit"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald ties a conversion to a journey only through an "},{"b":"anonymous visitor ID"},{"s":": a random ID the browser makes, such as "},{"code":"skv_"},{"s":" followed by 22 letters and digits. It holds no name, email or fingerprint."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"The script tag makes the ID and sends it with each event."}],[{"s":"It adds the ID to Calendly links and embeds as "},{"code":"utm_content"},{"s":", and Calendly sends it back in its webhook."}],[{"s":"For other tools, the ID is passed in a hidden field or a metadata value. "},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":" says how for each tool."}],[{"s":"Your site's lead push and lead database can carry the same ID."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The figures never match by IP address, and never link a new ID to an old one. A visitor ID is a "},{"i":"browser"},{"s":", not a person: one person on a phone and a laptop is two browsers. The person search can show, apart from the figures, the visits that sent a form at a lead's time: a match by time, never certain. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Visitor IDs are off by default. An owner or admin turns them on per site in "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Sites > Script tag"},{"s":". "},{"a":"Integrations","href":"#settings/integrations"},{"s":" says whether they are on. Your privacy notice must say so, and some places need consent first. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Without visitor IDs, conversions are still counted, but there are no journeys, no abandoned counts, no assisted sources and no pages seen before converting. With them off, Skald keeps no visitor ID from any road: not from the script tag, not from a webhook's "},{"code":"vid"},{"s":", and not from your lead database's session column."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Goals"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald's goals are not set on Pipeline. A goal is a page event, such as \"demo booked\" or \"sign-up sent\", shown per 100 visits by source on "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Events","href":"#sales/events"},{"s":". Admins choose them in "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Sites > Goals"},{"s":". See "},{"a":"Funnels and goals","href":"#help?part=funnels-and-goals"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"When a figure is missing"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Withheld"},{"s":": every figure is counted twice, by two separate roads. When they disagree on a day, that day is withheld and left out of every sum. The tab says which days and why."}],[{"b":"Not recorded"},{"s":": days before a source was set up are not recorded, never zero."}],[{"b":"Too few to say"},{"s":": no rate is given over fewer than 10."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Finding one person"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Owners and admins can type an IP address, an email, a lead's number or a visitor ID in "},{"b":"Find a person"},{"s":" on "},{"a":"Leads & sales > People","href":"#sales/people"},{"s":", or in the search box at the top (or "},{"b":"Ctrl K"},{"s":"). It shows that person's visits, leads and conversions, spam, test, cancelled and removed ones too, linked together. Each search is written to the audit log. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Removing a person's data"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To delete one person's data (for a privacy request), ask the person who runs your Skald server. They run "},{"code":"skald forget"},{"s":" with the email, IP address, visitor ID or lead reference. It deletes their conversions, the removed rows, their name and email, and the visits kept with their address."}]}]},{"id":"tracking-script","title":"The tracking script","summary":[{"s":"How to add Skald's one-line "},{"code":"skald.js"},{"s":" tag to your pages, what it sees, what it never collects, and how to check that it works."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"What it is for"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Your server log already counts visits and pages. It cannot see what happens "},{"i":"inside"},{"s":" a page: a form started and not sent, a phone link clicked, a demo booked in a widget. The "},{"code":"skald.js"},{"s":" tag reports those."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"It is under 6 KB of plain JavaScript."}],[{"s":"It sends events to your own site's address, never to a third party."}],[{"s":"It uses no cookies, unless you ask it to share an ID across subdomains (below)."}],[{"s":"Skald's figures from the log never depend on it. Without the tag, you lose nothing you already have."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Add the tag"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"You need to be an admin of the site."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Integrations"},{"s":", or go to "},{"a":"Integrations","href":"#settings/integrations"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"If you manage more than one site, choose the site at the top."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"The script tag"},{"s":", tick the options you need (see \"Options\" below). The tag updates as you tick."}],[{"s":"Copy the tag."}],[{"s":"Paste it into the "},{"code":"<head>"},{"s":" of every page of your site. In most site builders this is a \"custom code\" or \"head code\" setting that applies to all pages."}],[{"s":"Publish your site."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The tag looks like this. Always copy yours from the page, because the address and site name are your own:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"<script src=\"https://www.example.com/traffic-js/skald.js\" data-site=\"example.com\" defer></script>"},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"The tag only works when your web server passes two addresses to Skald: "},{"code":"/traffic-js/skald.js"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"/traffic-beacon"},{"s":". The person who runs your Skald server sets this up once."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If the Integrations page is not in your Settings menu, your server does not use accounts, or you are not an admin. Ask the person who runs your Skald server for the tag."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"More than one site"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Since Skald 2.9.0, every site on your Skald can use the tag, not only the first one."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Each site's events go to that site. Skald knows the site by the address the page is on."}],[{"s":"A site added from the dashboard takes events from its own "},{"b":"Host names"},{"s":" ("},{"a":"Sites","href":"#settings/sites"},{"s":", under "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Sites"},{"s":"). Nothing else to set. This works once the person who runs your Skald server has turned the tag on for the first site."}],[{"s":"A host name you add there works within a minute."}],[{"s":"Anonymous visitor IDs (below) are set per site. One site can have them on and another off."}]]},{"t":"h3","text":"A site on another server"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The tag sends events to the address of the page it is on. So when your site runs on a different server from Skald, that server must pass two addresses on to Skald: "},{"code":"/traffic-js/skald.js"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"/traffic-beacon"},{"s":". Your developer or host sets this up once (a \"reverse proxy\" or \"rewrite\"). The tag then loads from your own site:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"<script src=\"/traffic-js/skald.js\" data-site=\"example.net\" defer></script>"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The person who runs your Skald server must also tell it to trust your site's server for the visitor's address. Without that, every visitor looks like one address, and the limit on events per visitor applies to all of them together. Skald uses the address only in memory and never keeps it."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Options"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Tick box on the page"}],[{"s":"Adds to the tag"}],[{"s":"What it does"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Wait for consent"}],[{"code":"data-consent=\"required\""}],[{"s":"sends nothing and keeps no ID until your consent banner says yes"}]],[[{"s":"Share across subdomains"}],[{"code":"data-share-subdomains=\"true\""}],[{"code":"www."},{"s":" and "},{"code":"app."},{"s":" see the same anonymous ID, kept in a first-party cookie"}]],[[{"s":"Other domains you own"}],[{"code":"data-link-domains=\"...\""}],[{"s":"links to those domains carry the anonymous ID"}]],[[{"s":"Accept the ID from your other domains"}],[{"code":"data-accept-id=\"true\""}],[{"s":"this site takes the ID a link from your other domains brought (below)"}]]]},{"t":"h2","text":"What it tracks by itself"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Once the tag is on a page, it reports these events with no extra work:"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Event"}],[{"s":"When"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Page view"}],[{"s":"the page loads, and each time a single-page app changes the address"}]],[[{"s":"Form started"}],[{"s":"a field of a form is first used (once per form per page)"}]],[[{"s":"Form sent"}],[{"s":"a form is submitted"}]],[[{"s":"Sign-up started, Sign-up sent"}],[{"s":"the same, for a form marked "},{"code":"data-skald=\"signup\""}]],[[{"s":"Contact sent"}],[{"s":"a form marked "},{"code":"data-skald=\"contact\""},{"s":" is submitted"}]],[[{"s":"Early access sent"}],[{"s":"a form marked "},{"code":"data-skald=\"waitlist\""},{"s":" is submitted"}]],[[{"s":"Phone click"}],[{"s":"a "},{"code":"tel:"},{"s":" link is clicked (never the number)"}]],[[{"s":"Email click"}],[{"s":"a "},{"code":"mailto:"},{"s":" link is clicked (never the address)"}]],[[{"s":"Link out"}],[{"s":"a link to another site is clicked (the other site's name only)"}]],[[{"s":"Button click"}],[{"s":"an element marked "},{"code":"data-skald-cta=\"<name>\""},{"s":" is clicked"}]],[[{"s":"Read ¾"}],[{"s":"the reader scrolls to three quarters of the page (once per page)"}]],[[{"s":"Copied"}],[{"s":"text is copied from the page (once per page; never the text)"}]],[[{"s":"Not found"}],[{"s":"a page marked "},{"code":"data-skald=\"404\""},{"s":" is shown, such as your \"page not found\" page"}]],[[{"s":"Calendly opened, time chosen, booked"}],[{"s":"inside a Calendly embed on your page"}]],[[{"s":"Cal.com opened, booked"}],[{"s":"inside a Cal.com embed"}]],[[{"s":"HubSpot meeting booked"}],[{"s":"inside a HubSpot meetings embed"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A form records only its own "},{"code":"id"},{"s":" or "},{"code":"name"},{"s":", such as "},{"code":"contact"},{"s":". It never reads what a person typed."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Marking forms and buttons"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"To track a button or link by name, add "},{"code":"data-skald-cta=\"pricing_top\""},{"s":" to it. It is reported as a Button click named "},{"code":"pricing_top"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"To count a form as a sign-up, add "},{"code":"data-skald=\"signup\""},{"s":" to the form."}],[{"s":"To count a form as a contact form, add "},{"code":"data-skald=\"contact\""},{"s":"; for an early-access or waiting list form, "},{"code":"data-skald=\"waitlist\""},{"s":". Starting either one still counts as Form started."}],[{"s":"To leave a form out, add "},{"code":"data-skald=\"off\""},{"s":". Search forms ("},{"code":"role=\"search\""},{"s":") are always left out."}],[{"s":"To count your \"page not found\" page, add "},{"code":"data-skald=\"404\""},{"s":" to its "},{"code":"<body>"},{"s":", or put "},{"code":"<div data-skald=\"404\" hidden></div>"},{"s":" anywhere on it. This also works in a single-page app."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"A form whose own code refuses the submit (for example, a missing field) still counts as sent. If that matters, your developer can send the event only after success: "},{"code":"skald('track', 'form_submit', {id: 'contact'})"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"What it does not track by itself"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Two events on "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Events","href":"#sales/events"},{"s":" come only from your site's own code: "},{"b":"Demo opened"},{"s":" ("},{"code":"book_demo_open"},{"s":") and "},{"b":"Demo booked"},{"s":" ("},{"code":"demo_booked"},{"s":"). The Events tab marks them \"sent by your own code\". Your developer sends them when your own booking step opens and succeeds:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"skald('track', 'demo_booked', {id: 'header'})"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A booking made inside a Calendly, Cal.com or HubSpot embed is already counted by the tag as Calendly booked, Cal.com booked or HubSpot meeting booked."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Time on page, pages per visit and one-page visits come from your server log, not from the tag."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What it never collects"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"No text a person typed, and no form field's value."}],[{"s":"No phone number or email address from a link."}],[{"s":"No IP address and no browser details are stored. Skald uses the address only in memory, to find the country and to limit abuse, and then drops it."}],[{"s":"No third-party code, and nothing sent anywhere but your own site."}],[{"s":"No fingerprinting."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"With visitor IDs on, the tag also keeps one random ID per browser (below). It holds no name or email."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Anonymous visitor IDs"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Visitor IDs let Skald follow one browser's anonymous journey up to a conversion. They make \"abandoned\", \"assisted\" and \"pages seen before converting\" possible. See "},{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"They are "},{"b":"off by default"},{"s":". The person who runs your Skald server turns them on per site."}],[{"s":"The Integrations page says, under the tag, whether they are on for your site."}],[{"s":"When they are off, the tag makes no ID at all and stores nothing in the browser."}],[{"s":"When they are on, the ID is kept in the browser's local storage. With \"Share across subdomains\", it is also kept in a first-party cookie called "},{"code":"skald_vid"},{"s":" for up to 400 days."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Turn visitor IDs on only when your privacy notice says so. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Consent and Do Not Track"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control"},{"s":": when the browser sends either one, the tag does nothing at all. No ID, no storage, no event."}],[{"b":"Consent first"},{"s":": in places that need consent before any ID (the EU, Quebec, often the rest of Canada), tick "},{"b":"Wait for consent"},{"s":". The tag then waits."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"When the visitor agrees, your consent banner must call this on every page:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"skald('consent', true)"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If the visitor says no, or withdraws consent, call "},{"code":"skald('consent', false)"},{"s":". This deletes the ID, the cookie and the stored source in that browser."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To call "},{"code":"skald"},{"s":" before the tag has loaded, your developer can put this line before the tag:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"<script>window.skald=window.skald||function(){(skald.q=skald.q||[]).push(arguments)}</script>"},{"t":"h2","text":"Your other domains (data-link-domains)"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If your visitors move between domains you own, such as "},{"code":"example.com"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"app.example.net"},{"s":", type the other domains in "},{"b":"Other domains you own"},{"s":", separated by commas."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"When a visitor clicks a link to one of them, the tag adds "},{"code":"?skv=<the visitor ID>"},{"s":" to the link."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"On the other domain, the same tag picks the ID up, so the visit continues the same anonymous journey:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Put the tag on the other domain's pages too (it can report to the same site, or to its own)."}],[{"s":"On that domain's tag, either list your first domain in "},{"b":"Other domains you own"},{"s":" (for example "},{"code":"example.com"},{"s":"), or tick "},{"b":"Accept the ID from your other domains"},{"s":" ("},{"code":"data-accept-id=\"true\""},{"s":")."}],[{"s":"Publish both."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"When a page opens with a valid "},{"code":"skv"},{"s":" in its address, the tag keeps that ID as the visitor's ID and takes "},{"code":"skv"},{"s":" out of the address bar, so it is not bookmarked or shared. Without "},{"code":"data-accept-id"},{"s":", it takes the ID only when the visitor came from a domain listed in "},{"b":"Other domains you own"},{"s":"; any other "},{"code":"skv"},{"s":" is ignored and left alone."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"With "},{"b":"Wait for consent"},{"s":", the ID is kept only after "},{"code":"skald('consent', true)"},{"s":". The address is cleaned at once either way."}],[{"s":"With Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control, the tag does nothing, so "},{"code":"skv"},{"s":" stays in the address."}],[{"s":"If your other domain does not run the tag, its own code can read "},{"code":"skv"},{"s":" and pass it to Skald, for example as "},{"code":"vid"},{"s":" in your site's lead push. See "},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"For subdomains of one domain ("},{"code":"www."},{"s":" and "},{"code":"app."},{"s":"), tick "},{"b":"Share across subdomains"},{"s":" instead. If the shared cookie does not work on your host (some free hosting addresses refuse it), the ID still works on each subdomain on its own."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Calendly links get utm_content"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"With visitor IDs on, the tag adds the visitor ID to every Calendly embed and Calendly link on your page, as "},{"code":"utm_content=<the visitor ID>"},{"s":". Calendly sends this back in its webhook, so the booking joins the visitor's journey."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"If a Calendly link already has a "},{"code":"utm_content"},{"s":", the tag leaves it alone. That booking then has no journey."}],[{"s":"This works for Calendly iframes, inline widgets and plain links. A popup opened only from your own JavaScript is not changed."}],[{"s":"You also need the Calendly webhook. See "},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":", section \"Calendly\"."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Check that it works"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open your site in a normal browser window. Make sure Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control are off in that browser, or the tag sends nothing."}],[{"s":"Open a page, click a link and start a form."}],[{"s":"In Skald, open "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Events","href":"#sales/events"},{"s":" and choose "},{"b":"Today"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"You should see \"Today so far, not yet checked\" and your events. Today's events are checked after midnight."}],[{"s":"At the bottom of the Events tab, a line says what the beacon took in today: accepted, declined, from machines, from your own addresses, refused."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Your own office is likely marked as internal traffic. Its events are kept apart as \"ours\" and not shown with people's. Test from a phone on mobile data, or see "},{"a":"Internal traffic","href":"#help?part=internal-traffic"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If you know your browser's developer tools, open the Network panel. Each event is a request to "},{"code":"/traffic-beacon"},{"s":". An answer of 204 means it was counted. An answer of 202 means it was taken and nothing was kept, which is normal for page views when visitor IDs are off."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"If nothing shows"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"The tag is not on the page: view the page's source and look for "},{"code":"skald.js"},{"s":"."}],[{"code":"/traffic-js/skald.js"},{"s":" does not load: the web server is not set up for it. Ask the person who runs your Skald server."}],[{"s":"Requests to "},{"code":"/traffic-beacon"},{"s":" are refused (403): the page's address is not on the server's list of allowed origins. For a site added from the dashboard, check that the page's exact host name (with or without "},{"code":"www."},{"s":") is in its "},{"b":"Host names"},{"s":" under "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Sites"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Your browser sends Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control."}],[{"s":"The tag waits for consent and your banner never calls "},{"code":"skald('consent', true)"},{"s":"."}]]}]},{"id":"webhooks","title":"Webhooks","summary":[{"s":"How to connect Calendly, Cal.com, HubSpot, Typeform, Stripe, Zapier, Make and your own site to Skald, so bookings, forms and payments show under Leads & sales. Also how Skald can send conversions out to your CRM."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"How it works"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each tool gets its own address in Skald and its own secret. When something happens (a booking, a payment, a form), the tool sends a signed message to that address. Skald checks the signature, records the conversion once, and shows it on "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Pipeline","href":"#sales/pipeline"},{"s":" (with "},{"b":"Count from: Tools"},{"s":") and, for a booking or a payment, on "},{"a":"Bookings","href":"#sales/bookings"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"All of this is set up on one page: "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Integrations"},{"s":", or "},{"a":"Integrations","href":"#settings/integrations"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"You need to be an admin or owner of the site's organisation. Viewers do not see this page."}],[{"s":"The page needs a server with accounts. Without it, the page says so, and the person who runs your Skald server sets up hooks on the server instead."}],[{"s":"If you manage more than one site, choose the site at the top first."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"The Integrations page"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"At the top, "},{"b":"Status"},{"s":" lists each road into Skald for this site, with "},{"b":"OK"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Needs attention"},{"s":" (and what to do) or "},{"b":"Off"},{"s":": the hook receiver, the script tag, each hook that is set up, one lead sent by two tools, and the lead database. The server's doctor command ("},{"code":"skald doctor"},{"s":"; Docker: "},{"code":"docker exec skald skald doctor"},{"s":") shows the same lines, and checks the rest of the install too."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Incoming hooks"},{"s":", each tool has a box with:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Its "},{"b":"address"},{"s":", with a copy button. It looks like "},{"code":"https://analytics.example.com/traffic-hooks/example.com/calendly"},{"s":". Always copy yours from the page."}],[{"s":"A badge: "},{"b":"no secret"},{"s":", "},{"b":"secret set"},{"s":", or "},{"b":"set (environment ...)"},{"s":" when the secret is kept on the server."}],[{"s":"Its state in words: "},{"b":"needs a secret"},{"s":", "},{"b":"never received"},{"s":" (set up, but nothing has come, not even a test), "},{"b":"ready"},{"s":" (a test passed, nothing real yet), or "},{"b":"last received 2 h ago"},{"s":". When the last message was refused, it says why and what to do."}],[{"b":"Make secret"},{"s":" (or "},{"b":"Rotate secret"},{"s":" once there is one), for the tools that take a secret Skald makes."}],[{"b":"Paste the signing secret from ..."},{"s":", for the tools that make their own secret (Stripe, HubSpot). Calendly, Cal.com and Typeform have both: use either one."}],[{"b":"Send a test event"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"Remove"},{"s":", once the hook has a secret."}],[{"b":"Last deliveries"},{"s":": the last 50 messages, with when, the answer, the outcome and any detail."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A hook does nothing until it has a secret. Without one, its address answers \"not found\"."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"The secret"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Who makes the secret depends on the tool:"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Tool"}],[{"s":"The secret"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Your site's server (lead), Zapier, Make, n8n (json)"}],[{"s":"Skald makes it: "},{"b":"Make secret"}]],[[{"s":"Calendly, Cal.com, Typeform"}],[{"s":"Either one: "},{"b":"Make secret"},{"s":" and give it to the tool, or paste the tool's own"}]],[[{"s":"Stripe, HubSpot"}],[{"s":"The tool makes it: "},{"b":"Paste the signing secret from ..."}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To make a secret in Skald:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Make secret"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"The secret is shown once, with the address. Copy both."}],[{"s":"Paste the secret into the other tool (each section below says where)."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"I have copied it"},{"s":". The secret is not shown again."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To paste a tool's own secret:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Copy the signing secret in the other tool (each section below says where)."}],[{"s":"In that tool's box in Skald, paste it into "},{"b":"Paste the signing secret from ..."},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Save secret"},{"s":". The box says "},{"b":"secret set"},{"s":". Skald never shows the secret again, not even to you."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To replace a pasted secret, paste the new one and save again."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Treat a secret like a password. Never put it in an email, a chat, a ticket or a shared document. Anyone with it can send fake conversions. If one leaks, press "},{"b":"Rotate secret"},{"s":" (or make a new secret in the tool and paste it): the old one stops working at once, and you give the new one to the tool."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If the box says "},{"b":"set (environment ...)"},{"s":", the secret is kept on the server. It cannot be made, pasted or removed on this page: ask the person who runs your Skald server."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"The test button"},{"t":"p","in":[{"b":"Send a test event"},{"s":" sends a signed sample to Skald's own receiver for that tool. It checks the signature and reads the sample, then keeps nothing and counts nothing. The page says \"the test was signed, received and read\", and what a real message would keep: the action, its stage, the source, country and device, and whether the visitor ID is kept. With visitor IDs off for the site, the visitor ID is dropped, as it is for a real message. The test shows as \"test, read and not kept\" in Last deliveries."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The server has the same test: "},{"code":"skald hooks test example.com lead"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The test checks Skald's side only. To check the other tool, use its own \"send test\" button, if it has one, and look at Last deliveries."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Calendly"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Calendly sends webhooks on its paid plans (Standard or higher). It has no screen for them: they are made through Calendly's API, usually by a developer."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"In Skald, open the "},{"b":"Calendly"},{"s":" box, press "},{"b":"Make secret"},{"s":", and copy the address and the secret."}],[{"s":"Make a webhook subscription in Calendly with that address. Use the secret as the subscription's "},{"b":"signing key"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Choose these events: "},{"code":"invitee.created"},{"s":", "},{"code":"invitee.canceled"},{"s":", "},{"code":"invitee_no_show.created"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If your subscription already has a signing key from Calendly, paste that key into "},{"b":"Paste the signing secret from Calendly"},{"s":" instead of making one."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A developer can make the subscription with one request:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"curl -X POST https://api.calendly.com/webhook_subscriptions \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer <your-calendly-token>\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"url\": \"https://analytics.example.com/traffic-hooks/example.com/calendly\",\n       \"events\": [\"invitee.created\", \"invitee.canceled\", \"invitee_no_show.created\"],\n       \"organization\": \"https://api.calendly.com/organizations/<your-organization-id>\",\n       \"scope\": \"organization\", \"signing_key\": \"<your-secret>\"}'"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"What Skald records: a booking (Demos, completed), a cancellation (cancelled, or rescheduled when Calendly says so) and a no-show. To join a booking to the visitor's journey, the tracking script adds the visitor ID to Calendly links as "},{"code":"utm_content"},{"s":". See "},{"a":"The tracking script","href":"#help?part=tracking-script"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Only some event types"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"One Calendly account often books for several businesses, and a Calendly webhook cannot be limited to some event types. So tell Skald which are this site's:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"In the "},{"b":"Calendly"},{"s":" box, find "},{"b":"Only these Calendly event types"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Enter one per line: the event type's address from Calendly's API ("},{"code":"https://api.calendly.com/event_types/..."},{"s":"), or the booking page's name at the end of its link ("},{"code":"product-demo"},{"s":" in "},{"code":"https://calendly.com/you/product-demo"},{"s":")."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Save event types"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Any other event type is answered \"OK\" and left out: nothing is kept, and Last deliveries shows \"not a conversion\" with the event type it named, so you can copy it. A no-show is kept when its booking was kept. Leave the box empty to keep every event. Calendly does not send the booking page's name, so Skald compares it with the event type's name (\"Product demo\" is "},{"code":"product-demo"},{"s":"). If you rename the event type, use its address instead. See "},{"a":"Demo bookings","href":"#help?part=demo-bookings"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Cal.com"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"In Skald, open the "},{"b":"Cal.com"},{"s":" box, press "},{"b":"Make secret"},{"s":", and copy the address and the secret."}],[{"s":"In Cal.com, go to "},{"b":"Settings > Developer > Webhooks > New"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"Subscriber URL"},{"s":": paste the address."}],[{"b":"Event triggers"},{"s":": Booking Created, Booking Cancelled, Booking Rescheduled."}],[{"b":"Secret"},{"s":": paste the secret. Save."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If the Cal.com webhook already has a secret of its own, paste it into "},{"b":"Paste the signing secret from Cal.com"},{"s":" in Skald instead."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To join a booking to the journey, pass the visitor ID in the embed as "},{"code":"metadata[skv]"},{"s":", or add a hidden booking question named "},{"code":"skv"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To keep only some event types, enter their ids ("},{"code":"1234"},{"s":") or names ("},{"code":"30min"},{"s":") in "},{"b":"Only these Cal.com event types"},{"s":", as for Calendly above."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"HubSpot"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"HubSpot signs its messages with your HubSpot app's "},{"b":"client secret"},{"s":". Skald cannot make one for it."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"In your HubSpot app, open "},{"b":"Auth"},{"s":" and copy the "},{"b":"Client secret"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"In Skald's "},{"b":"HubSpot"},{"s":" box, paste it into "},{"b":"Paste the signing secret from HubSpot"},{"s":" and press "},{"b":"Save secret"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"In your HubSpot app, open "},{"b":"Webhooks"},{"s":" and set the "},{"b":"Target URL"},{"s":" to the address from the "},{"b":"HubSpot"},{"s":" box."}],[{"s":"Subscribe to "},{"code":"contact.creation"},{"s":" (counted as a Contact form), to "},{"code":"object.creation"},{"s":" for meetings (counted as a Demo), and to "},{"code":"deal.propertyChange"},{"s":" for "},{"code":"dealstage"},{"s":" (a deal moved to closed won counts as a won Deal)."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"You can also use a HubSpot workflow's "},{"b":"Send a webhook"},{"s":" action, signed by the same app. Skald counts it as a Contact form. To count it as something else, add a property "},{"code":"skald_action"},{"s":", for example "},{"code":"demo"},{"s":" in a \"meeting booked\" workflow. Skald reads the properties "},{"code":"skv"},{"s":" (the visitor ID) and "},{"code":"utm_*"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"If your HubSpot account cannot sign a workflow webhook, send it through Zapier or Make instead (below)."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Typeform"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"In Skald, open the "},{"b":"Typeform"},{"s":" box, press "},{"b":"Make secret"},{"s":", and copy the address and the secret."}],[{"s":"In Typeform, open your form, then "},{"b":"Connect > Webhooks > Add a webhook"},{"s":". Paste the address."}],[{"s":"Open the webhook's settings ("},{"b":"Edit"},{"s":") and paste the secret into "},{"b":"Secret"},{"s":". Save, and turn the webhook on."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If the Typeform webhook already has a secret of its own, paste it into "},{"b":"Paste the signing secret from Typeform"},{"s":" in Skald instead."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Typeform sends every response. Skald counts each as a Contact form, completed. To join it to the journey, add a hidden field "},{"code":"skv"},{"s":" to the form and fill it in the embed. Hidden "},{"code":"utm_*"},{"s":" fields give the last touch. Skald never reads the answers."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Stripe"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Stripe makes its own signing secret, which starts with "},{"code":"whsec_"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"In Stripe, go to "},{"b":"Developers > Webhooks > Add endpoint"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"Endpoint URL"},{"s":": paste the address from the "},{"b":"Stripe"},{"s":" box."}],[{"s":"Events: "},{"code":"checkout.session.completed"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Save, then reveal the endpoint's "},{"b":"Signing secret"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"In Skald's "},{"b":"Stripe"},{"s":" box, paste it into "},{"b":"Paste the signing secret from Stripe"},{"s":" and press "},{"b":"Save secret"},{"s":". Skald cannot make a secret for Stripe."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald counts a paid Checkout as a Payment. A Checkout paid by a delayed method counts as started first, then paid. To join it to the journey, set the visitor ID as the Checkout Session's "},{"code":"client_reference_id"},{"s":", or as "},{"code":"metadata.skv"},{"s":". Skald never reads customer details."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Zapier and Make"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Use the "},{"b":"Zapier, Make, n8n (json)"},{"s":" box. This hook takes the same fields as your own site's lead push (next section), signed the same way."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Make secret"},{"s":" in that box, and copy the address and the secret."}],[{"s":"Keep the secret in the tool's own secure storage, not in a plain text step."}],[{"s":"In "},{"b":"Zapier"},{"s":", add a \"Code by Zapier\" step that signs the body and posts it (the example in the next section works)."}],[{"s":"In "},{"b":"Make"},{"s":", use the HTTP module. Set the header "},{"code":"X-Skald-Signature"},{"s":" to "},{"code":"t={{timestamp}},v1={{sha256(timestamp + \".\" + body; \"hex\"; secret)}}"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"One message can carry one record, a list of them, or "},{"code":"{\"records\": [...]}"},{"s":", up to 100."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Your own site's lead push"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If your website's database is not read by Skald directly, your site's server can tell Skald each time a lead is made. Use the "},{"b":"Your site's server (lead)"},{"s":" box."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Make secret"},{"s":", and copy the address and the secret."}],[{"s":"Give both to your developer. They keep the secret in the server's settings, never in the code."}],[{"s":"Your server sends a "},{"code":"POST"},{"s":" with a JSON body and this header:"}]]},{"t":"pre","text":"X-Skald-Signature: t=<unix seconds>,v1=<hex HMAC-SHA256 of \"<t>.<raw body>\">"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The key is the secret. Skald refuses a time more than 5 minutes off its own clock."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Field"}],[{"s":"Needed"}],[{"s":"What"}]],"rows":[[[{"code":"external_ref"}],[{"s":"yes"}],[{"s":"the lead's own ID in your site"}]],[[{"code":"action"}],[{"s":"yes"}],[{"s":"a short word: "},{"code":"demo"},{"s":", "},{"code":"signup"},{"s":", "},{"code":"contact"},{"s":", "},{"code":"trial"}]],[[{"code":"stage"}],[{"s":"no"}],[{"code":"started"},{"s":", "},{"code":"completed"},{"s":" (the default), "},{"code":"cancelled"},{"s":", "},{"code":"rescheduled"},{"s":", "},{"code":"no_show"},{"s":", "},{"code":"paid"}]],[[{"code":"at"}],[{"s":"no"}],[{"s":"when, as an ISO time with its offset, such as "},{"code":"2026-09-25T14:30:00-04:00"},{"s":"; default: when it arrived. A time without an offset is read in the site's time zone, and Last deliveries says so"}]],[[{"code":"vid"}],[{"s":"no"}],[{"s":"the visitor ID the page had"}]],[[{"code":"first_touch"},{"s":", "},{"code":"last_touch"}],[{"s":"no"}],[{"s":"referrer, landing page, "},{"code":"utm_*"},{"s":" tags, ad click ids, time"}]],[[{"code":"country"},{"s":" or "},{"code":"ip"}],[{"s":"no"}],[{"s":"two letters, or the visitor's address: Skald finds the country and drops the address"}]],[[{"code":"device"},{"s":" or "},{"code":"user_agent"}],[{"s":"no"}],[{"s":"Desktop, Mobile or Tablet, or the browser string: Skald works out the device and drops it"}]],[[{"code":"name"},{"s":", "},{"code":"email"}],[{"s":"no"}],[{"s":"kept only when the site's "},{"b":"Leads' names and emails"},{"s":" is "},{"b":"full"},{"s":"; otherwise dropped"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A short test from a terminal:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"BODY='{\"external_ref\":\"L-1001\",\"action\":\"demo\"}'\nT=$(date +%s)\nSIG=$(printf '%s.%s' \"$T\" \"$BODY\" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac \"<your-secret>\" -hex | sed 's/^.* //')\ncurl -X POST 'https://analytics.example.com/traffic-hooks/example.com/lead' \\\n  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H \"X-Skald-Signature: t=$T,v1=$SIG\" --data-raw \"$BODY\""},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"If Skald already reads your website's lead database, you do not need the lead push. See "},{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The full how-to, with examples in curl, Node, Python and PHP, retries and backfilling: "},{"a":"Send leads from your backend in 5 minutes","href":"#help?part=leads-from-your-backend"},{"s":". If your server and Skald share a machine behind Cloudflare, post to Skald's local address: the guide says how."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What Skald stores, and what it drops"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Kept"},{"s":": the action, its stage, the time, the tool, the tool's own reference, the visitor ID (only when the site has visitor IDs on), and the source, campaign, landing page, country and device when known."}],[{"b":"Kept for checking"},{"s":": a copy of each verified message, cut down to the fields Skald reads. It is kept 400 days, so every figure can be counted a second time."}],[{"b":"Always dropped"},{"s":": IP addresses, browser strings, phone numbers, extra email addresses, form answers, customer details, and Calendly's cancel and reschedule links."}],[{"b":"Names and emails"},{"s":": kept only when "},{"b":"Leads' names and emails"},{"s":" is "},{"b":"full"},{"s":" ("},{"b":"Settings > Data retention > People"},{"s":"). That is the default for a new install. An install upgraded from before 2.4.0 drops them until an admin turns it on. Your privacy notice must say so. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"The delivery log"},{"s":": when, the outcome and the answer, never the message itself. Kept 90 days."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Duplicates and retries"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"A tool sends again when it does not get an \"OK\" answer. This is harmless."}],[{"s":"Skald keeps each conversion once per tool, reference and stage. A repeat is answered \"OK\" and shows as \"already had it\" in Last deliveries. Nothing is counted twice."}],[{"s":"Cal.com and Typeform sign no time, so Skald also remembers each message for 30 days and ignores an exact repeat."}],[{"b":"One lead, one road."},{"s":" Each tool keeps its own record, so the same lead sent through two tools (your lead push and Zapier, or the lead push and the lead database) counts twice. The "},{"b":"Status"},{"s":" list names any lead that arrived from two tools: send each lead one way only."}],[{"s":"If Skald cannot save a message, it answers with an error, and the tool sends it again later."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Remove an integration"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Delete the webhook in the other tool (Calendly, Cal.com, HubSpot, Typeform, Stripe, Zapier or Make)."}],[{"s":"In Skald, press "},{"b":"Remove"},{"s":" in that tool's box, then "},{"b":"Yes, remove"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald deletes the hook's secret. Its address then refuses every message, as if it had never been set up. "},{"b":"Last deliveries"},{"s":" stays, and the removal is in the audit log. To use the tool again, make or paste a secret."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If the secret is kept on the server ("},{"b":"set (environment ...)"},{"s":"), there is no Remove button: ask the person who runs your Skald server."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Conversions already recorded stay. To delete one person's data, see "},{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Sending conversions out (outgoing webhooks)"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald can tell your CRM, Zapier, Make or Slack each time something happens. This is under "},{"b":"Outgoing webhooks"},{"s":" on the same page."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Add an outgoing webhook"},{"s":", paste the "},{"b":"Address"},{"s":". It must start with "},{"code":"https://"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Tick the "},{"b":"Events"},{"s":" you want: "},{"code":"conversion.started"},{"s":", "},{"code":"conversion.completed"},{"s":", "},{"code":"conversion.cancelled"},{"s":", "},{"code":"conversion.rescheduled"},{"s":", "},{"code":"conversion.no_show"},{"s":", "},{"code":"conversion.abandoned"},{"s":", "},{"code":"lead.won"},{"s":", "},{"code":"lead.lost"},{"s":", and "},{"code":"ai.reading_changed"},{"s":" (an AI assistant started or stopped reading a page, or visits likely sent by AI answers jumped or vanished: see the FAQ)."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Add webhook"},{"s":". Copy the secret shown once, and give it to the receiving tool so it can check each message."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Send a test"},{"s":" to check that the address answers."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"An "},{"code":"ai.reading_changed"},{"s":" message names the assistant, the pages, the days and the numbers, and is sent once per alert, only while alerts are on. Each conversion message names the action, its source, campaign, landing page, country, device, visits and time before converting, and the anonymous journey. It never holds a name or an email. A failed delivery is tried again for about 15 hours. Only conversions recorded after you add the webhook are sent. "},{"b":"Remove"},{"s":" stops it at once."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Troubleshooting"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open the tool's box and look at "},{"b":"Last deliveries"},{"s":". The "},{"b":"Outcome"},{"s":" column says what happened:"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Outcome"}],[{"s":"What it means"}],[{"s":"What to do"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"kept"}],[{"s":"recorded"}],[{"s":"nothing"}]],[[{"s":"already had it"}],[{"s":"a repeat of a message already kept"}],[{"s":"nothing"}]],[[{"s":"not a conversion"}],[{"s":"an event Skald does not count, or (with a detail \"other event type\") a Calendly or Cal.com event type this site does not keep"}],[{"s":"choose the events listed above; or add the event type to the list"}]],[[{"s":"test, read and not kept"}],[{"s":"a test"}],[{"s":"nothing"}]],[[{"s":"bad signature"}],[{"s":"the secret does not match, or the time is more than 5 minutes off"}],[{"s":"paste the secret again, or rotate it and give the new one; check the sender's clock"}]],[[{"s":"not readable"}],[{"s":"the message is not what this tool sends"}],[{"s":"check you used the address for the right tool"}]],[[{"s":"too large"}],[{"s":"the message is over 64 KB"}],[{"s":"send fewer records at once"}]],[[{"s":"too many"}],[{"s":"over 60 messages a minute"}],[{"s":"the tool will retry; send in smaller batches"}]],[[{"s":"error"}],[{"s":"Skald could not save it"}],[{"s":"the tool will retry; tell the person who runs your server if it repeats"}]]]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"No deliveries at all"},{"s":": the tool is not sending. Check the address is pasted exactly, and that the webhook is turned on in the tool."}],[{"b":"The box says \"no secret\""},{"s":": the address answers \"not found\" until a secret is set. A removed hook says this too."}],[{"b":"\"A Stripe signing secret starts with whsec_\""},{"s":": you copied something else, such as an API key. Copy the endpoint's "},{"b":"Signing secret"},{"s":" in Stripe."}],[{"b":"A red note says the site's hooks are not answered"},{"s":": this server does not report on that site yet."}],[{"b":"Bookings show but have no journey"},{"s":": the visitor ID did not reach the tool. Check visitor IDs are on, and the hidden field or "},{"code":"utm_content"},{"s":" above."}],[{"b":"HubSpot \"bad signature\" behind a proxy"},{"s":": the person who runs your server may need to set Skald's public address."}]]}]},{"id":"leads-from-your-backend","title":"Send leads from your backend in 5 minutes","summary":[{"s":"Your site's server tells Skald each time a lead is made, in one signed message. This guide has the steps and copy-paste examples in curl, Node, Python and PHP, with retries, and what to do when the backend sits on the same server as Skald."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"1. Make the secret"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"On the server:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"sudo skald hooks secret example.com lead"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Or in the dashboard: "},{"b":"Settings > Integrations > Your site's server (lead) > Make secret"},{"s":". Docker: "},{"code":"docker exec skald skald hooks secret example.com lead"},{"s":" (in Docker, run every "},{"code":"skald"},{"s":" command in this guide the same way, without "},{"code":"sudo"},{"s":")."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"It prints the secret once, and the address to post to. With "},{"code":"access.base_url"},{"s":" set, the address is the real one, such as "},{"code":"https://stats.example.com/traffic-hooks/example.com/lead"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Keep the secret in an environment variable on your backend, such as "},{"code":"SKALD_HOOK_SECRET"},{"s":". Never in the code, never in the browser."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"2. The body"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"One JSON object per lead:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"{\n  \"external_ref\": \"L-1001\",\n  \"action\": \"demo\",\n  \"stage\": \"completed\",\n  \"at\": \"2026-09-25T14:30:00-04:00\",\n  \"vid\": \"skv_Q2xhc3NpY0V4YW1wbGVJRA\",\n  \"first_touch\": {\"referrer\": \"https://www.google.com/\", \"landing\": \"/\", \"at\": \"2026-09-20T09:12:00Z\"},\n  \"last_touch\": {\"landing\": \"/pricing/\", \"utm_source\": \"newsletter\", \"utm_medium\": \"email\"}\n}"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Field"}],[],[]],"rows":[[[{"code":"external_ref"}],[{"s":"required"}],[{"s":"The lead's own id in your system. Keep it stable: the same lead always sends the same id"}]],[[{"code":"action"}],[{"s":"required"}],[{"s":"What was done, a short lowercase word: "},{"code":"demo"},{"s":", "},{"code":"contact"},{"s":", "},{"code":"signup"},{"s":", "},{"code":"trial"}]],[[{"code":"stage"}],[{"s":"default "},{"code":"completed"}],[{"code":"started"},{"s":", "},{"code":"completed"},{"s":", "},{"code":"cancelled"},{"s":", "},{"code":"rescheduled"},{"s":", "},{"code":"no_show"},{"s":", "},{"code":"paid"},{"s":", "},{"code":"won"},{"s":", "},{"code":"lost"}]],[[{"code":"at"}],[{"s":"default: when it arrived"}],[{"s":"When it happened. A full ISO time with its offset: "},{"code":"2026-09-25T14:30:00-04:00"},{"s":" or "},{"code":"2026-09-25T18:30:00Z"}]],[[{"code":"vid"}],[],[{"s":"The visitor ID the page had. Kept only when the site has visitor IDs on"}]],[[{"code":"first_touch"},{"s":", "},{"code":"last_touch"}],[],[{"s":"Where the visitor came from: "},{"code":"referrer"},{"s":", "},{"code":"landing"},{"s":", "},{"code":"utm_source"},{"s":", "},{"code":"utm_medium"},{"s":", "},{"code":"utm_campaign"},{"s":", "},{"code":"at"}]],[[{"code":"ip"},{"s":", "},{"code":"user_agent"}],[],[{"s":"Skald looks up the country and the device, then drops both"}]],[[{"code":"name"},{"s":", "},{"code":"email"}],[],[{"s":"Kept only when the site's "},{"b":"Leads' names and emails"},{"s":" is "},{"b":"full"},{"s":"; otherwise dropped"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Always send the offset. A time without one (\"2026-09-25\" or \"2026-09-25T14:30:00\") is read in the site's own time zone, and the delivery log says so. That guess is right only when your server writes local times in the same zone."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"3. Sign it and send it"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The header:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"X-Skald-Signature: t=<unix seconds>,v1=<hex HMAC-SHA256 of \"<t>.<raw body>\">"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The key is the secret. Sign the exact bytes you send. Skald refuses a "},{"code":"t"},{"s":" more than 5 minutes from its own clock, so keep the server's clock right."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each example below signs, posts, and tries again when the post fails."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"curl:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"URL='https://stats.example.com/traffic-hooks/example.com/lead'\nBODY='{\"external_ref\":\"L-1001\",\"action\":\"demo\",\"at\":\"2026-09-25T14:30:00-04:00\"}'\nfor wait in 0 5 30 120; do\n  sleep \"$wait\"\n  T=$(date +%s)\n  SIG=$(printf '%s.%s' \"$T\" \"$BODY\" | openssl dgst -sha256 -hmac \"$SKALD_HOOK_SECRET\" -hex | sed 's/^.* //')\n  CODE=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' -X POST \"$URL\" \\\n    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -H \"X-Skald-Signature: t=$T,v1=$SIG\" --data-raw \"$BODY\")\n  case \"$CODE\" in 2*) break ;; 400|401|404|413) echo \"refused: $CODE\"; break ;; esac\ndone"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Node (18 or later):"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"import crypto from \"node:crypto\";\n\nconst URL = \"https://stats.example.com/traffic-hooks/example.com/lead\";\n\nexport async function sendLead(lead) {\n  const body = JSON.stringify(lead);\n  for (const wait of [0, 5, 30, 120]) {\n    await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, wait * 1000));\n    const t = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000);\n    const sig = crypto.createHmac(\"sha256\", process.env.SKALD_HOOK_SECRET).update(`${t}.${body}`).digest(\"hex\");\n    try {\n      const res = await fetch(URL, { method: \"POST\", body,\n        headers: { \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"X-Skald-Signature\": `t=${t},v1=${sig}` } });\n      if (res.ok) return true;\n      if ([400, 401, 404, 413].includes(res.status)) return false;\n    } catch { /* the network: try again */ }\n  }\n  return false;\n}"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Python (standard library only):"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"import hashlib, hmac, json, os, time, urllib.error, urllib.request\n\nURL = \"https://stats.example.com/traffic-hooks/example.com/lead\"\n\ndef send_lead(lead: dict) -> bool:\n    body = json.dumps(lead).encode()\n    secret = os.environ[\"SKALD_HOOK_SECRET\"].encode()\n    for wait in (0, 5, 30, 120):\n        time.sleep(wait)\n        t = str(int(time.time()))\n        sig = hmac.new(secret, t.encode() + b\".\" + body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n        req = urllib.request.Request(URL, data=body, method=\"POST\", headers={\n            \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"X-Skald-Signature\": f\"t={t},v1={sig}\"})\n        try:\n            with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10):\n                return True\n        except urllib.error.HTTPError as why:\n            if why.code in (400, 401, 404, 413):\n                return False\n        except OSError:\n            pass\n    return False"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"PHP:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"function skald_send_lead(array $lead): bool {\n    $url = 'https://stats.example.com/traffic-hooks/example.com/lead';\n    $body = json_encode($lead);\n    foreach ([0, 5, 30, 120] as $wait) {\n        sleep($wait);\n        $t = time();\n        $sig = hash_hmac('sha256', $t . '.' . $body, getenv('SKALD_HOOK_SECRET'));\n        $ch = curl_init($url);\n        curl_setopt_array($ch, [CURLOPT_POST => true, CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS => $body,\n            CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER => true, CURLOPT_TIMEOUT => 10,\n            CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER => ['Content-Type: application/json', \"X-Skald-Signature: t=$t,v1=$sig\"]]);\n        curl_exec($ch);\n        $code = curl_getinfo($ch, CURLINFO_HTTP_CODE);\n        curl_close($ch);\n        if ($code >= 200 && $code < 300) return true;\n        if (in_array($code, [400, 401, 404, 413])) return false;\n    }\n    return false;\n}"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"In a web request, send the lead after the page has answered, or from a queue, so a slow answer never holds up your visitor."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"4. Retries are safe"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Try again on anything but a 2xx answer, and on a network error, with a growing wait. A repeat changes nothing: Skald keeps a conversion once per site, tool, "},{"code":"external_ref"},{"s":" and stage."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Do not retry a 400. The body is wrong: the answer says what, and so does the delivery log. Fix the body first."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"5. One tool per lead"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Send each lead through one road only. If the same lead also goes through Zapier (the "},{"code":"json"},{"s":" hook), or Skald also reads it from the lead database, it counts once per road. "},{"b":"Settings > Integrations > Status"},{"s":" flags such leads as \"One lead, two tools\"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"6. Backfill old leads"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Send each old lead with its original "},{"code":"at"},{"s":", with the offset. Then it lands on the day it happened."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Each hook takes at most 60 messages a minute by default ("},{"code":"hooks.per_minute"},{"s":"). Space them out, or retry on 429."}],[{"s":"Or send up to 100 at once through the "},{"code":"json"},{"s":" hook: "},{"code":"{\"records\": [ {...}, {...} ]}"},{"s":". Make its secret first, the same way."}],[{"s":"An "},{"code":"at"},{"s":" more than a day in the future is refused."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"7. Same server as Skald, behind Cloudflare"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"When your backend runs on the same server as Skald, and the public address goes through Cloudflare (or another CDN proxy), post to Skald's local address instead. Cloudflare can block a server that posts to its own public address: 403, error 1010, a bot check."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Skald runs"}],[{"s":"Post to"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"In Docker"}],[{"code":"http://127.0.0.1:8080/traffic-hooks/example.com/lead"},{"s":" (the port you published)"}]],[[{"s":"Installed with the install script"}],[{"code":"http://127.0.0.1:8766/traffic-hooks/example.com/lead"},{"s":" (the hook receiver itself)"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Or allow the path "},{"code":"/traffic-hooks/"},{"s":" in Cloudflare's security rules for your server. The signature is the same either way."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"8. Test it"},{"t":"pre","text":"sudo skald hooks test example.com lead"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"It posts a signed sample, marked as a test: read, never kept. It says what a real one would keep: the action, the stage, the source, and whether the visitor ID is kept. "},{"b":"Send a test event"},{"s":" on the Integrations page does the same."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Then send a real lead. The Integrations page shows \"last received 2 min ago (kept)\", and "},{"code":"sudo skald doctor"},{"s":" shows the hook as OK."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What Skald answers"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Answer"}],[{"s":"Means"}],[{"s":"Do"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"200"}],[{"s":"Taken: "},{"code":"{\"ok\":true,\"recorded\":1,\"duplicates\":0}"},{"s":". A repeat shows as a duplicate"}],[{"s":"Nothing"}]],[[{"s":"400"}],[{"s":"The body is not JSON, or a field is wrong (no "},{"code":"external_ref"},{"s":", a time that is not a time)"}],[{"s":"Fix the body; do not retry"}]],[[{"s":"401"}],[{"s":"The signature does not match, or "},{"code":"t"},{"s":" is more than 5 minutes off"}],[{"s":"Check the secret and the clock"}]],[[{"s":"404"}],[{"s":"No such site or tool, or the hook has no secret"}],[{"s":"Make the secret; check the address"}]],[[{"s":"413"}],[{"s":"The body is over 64 KiB"}],[{"s":"Send fewer records at once"}]],[[{"s":"429"}],[{"s":"Too many at once"}],[{"s":"Wait and try again"}]],[[{"s":"500"}],[{"s":"Not kept (disk or database)"}],[{"s":"Send it again"}]]]}]},{"id":"demo-bookings","title":"Demo bookings","summary":[{"s":"How booked calls from Calendly and Cal.com reach Skald, what each way can see, and how to keep only your own event types when one account books for several businesses."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"Three ways Calendly reaches Skald"},{"t":"table","head":[[],[{"s":"Embedded on your page"}],[{"s":"A link to calendly.com"}],[{"s":"The Calendly webhook"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Needs"}],[{"s":"The script tag"}],[{"s":"The script tag"}],[{"s":"A paid Calendly plan (Standard or higher) and the "},{"code":"calendly"},{"s":" hook"}]],[[{"s":"Opened the booking"}],[{"s":"Yes ("},{"code":"calendly_open"},{"s":")"}],[{"s":"No: only a click out to calendly.com"}],[{"s":"No"}]],[[{"s":"Chose a time"}],[{"s":"Yes ("},{"code":"calendly_time_selected"},{"s":")"}],[{"s":"No"}],[{"s":"No"}]],[[{"s":"Booked"}],[{"s":"Yes ("},{"code":"calendly_booked"},{"s":")"}],[{"s":"No"}],[{"s":"Yes"}]],[[{"s":"Cancelled, rescheduled, no-show"}],[{"s":"No"}],[{"s":"No"}],[{"s":"Yes"}]],[[{"s":"Booked off your site (a link in an email)"}],[{"s":"No"}],[{"s":"No"}],[{"s":"Yes"}]],[[{"s":"Joined to the visitor's journey"}],[{"s":"Yes, with visitor IDs on"}],[{"s":"With visitor IDs on, through "},{"code":"utm_content"}],[{"s":"Yes, through "},{"code":"utm_content"},{"s":", with visitor IDs on"}]]]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Embedded"},{"s":" means Calendly's inline widget or popup on your own page. The script tag listens to Calendly's own messages in the page."}],[{"b":"A link"},{"s":" sends the visitor away to calendly.com. The page sees only the click out. The script tag adds the visitor ID to the link as "},{"code":"utm_content"},{"s":", so the webhook can join the booking to the journey."}],[{"b":"The webhook"},{"s":" is Calendly telling Skald about each booking. It sees every booking, wherever it was made."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The best of both: embed the booking on your page, and turn on the webhook. Then you see opened, time chosen, booked, and what happened after."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Set up the Calendly webhook"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"In Skald: "},{"b":"Settings > Integrations > Calendly > Make secret"},{"s":". Copy the secret and the address."}],[{"s":"In Calendly: make a personal access token (on Calendly's integrations page, under API and webhooks)."}],[{"s":"Find your organisation's URI:"}]]},{"t":"pre","text":"curl -s https://api.calendly.com/users/me -H \"Authorization: Bearer $CALENDLY_TOKEN\""},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Make the subscription. The "},{"code":"signing_key"},{"s":" is Skald's secret:"}]],"start":4},{"t":"pre","text":"curl -sS -X POST https://api.calendly.com/webhook_subscriptions \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $CALENDLY_TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n  -d '{\"url\": \"https://stats.example.com/traffic-hooks/example.com/calendly\",\n       \"events\": [\"invitee.created\", \"invitee.canceled\", \"invitee_no_show.created\"],\n       \"organization\": \"https://api.calendly.com/organizations/<ORG>\",\n       \"scope\": \"organization\", \"signing_key\": \"<the hook secret>\"}'"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Send a test event"},{"s":" on the Integrations page. Then book a test call."}]],"start":5},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A booking counts as a demo completed; a cancellation as cancelled (or rescheduled, when Calendly says so); a no-show as no-show."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Keep only your own event types"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"One Calendly account often books for several businesses. A Calendly webhook cannot be limited to some event types: it sends every booking of the account. So Skald filters them."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"In "},{"b":"Settings > Integrations > Calendly"},{"s":", fill "},{"b":"Only these Calendly event types"},{"s":", one per line. Any of these works:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"The event type's URI: "},{"code":"https://api.calendly.com/event_types/AAAA1111"},{"s":". This always matches."}],[{"s":"Its id alone: "},{"code":"AAAA1111"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"The booking page's slug: "},{"code":"product-demo"},{"s":", or the page's address "},{"code":"https://calendly.com/example/product-demo"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Calendly does not send the booking page's slug. So Skald compares a slug with the event type's "},{"b":"name"},{"s":" written as a slug: \"Product demo\" becomes "},{"code":"product-demo"},{"s":". If you rename the event type, a slug stops matching. The URI never does."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"To find the URI:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"curl -s \"https://api.calendly.com/event_types?user=<your user URI>\" -H \"Authorization: Bearer $CALENDLY_TOKEN\""},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Or wait for a booking of another type: the delivery log names each event type it left out, so you can copy the URI from there."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"What happens then:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"A booking of a listed type is kept, as before."}],[{"s":"A booking of another type is answered 200, so Calendly does not send it again. It shows as \"not a conversion\" in Last deliveries, with the detail \"other event type\" and the type it named. Nothing else is kept: no conversion, no copy of the message."}],[{"s":"A no-show names only the person, not the event type. It is kept when its booking was kept."}],[{"s":"An empty list keeps every booking."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"On a server without accounts, set it in the config:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"hooks:\n  calendly_event_types: [https://api.calendly.com/event_types/AAAA1111]"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"With PyYAML installed, the nested form works too: "},{"code":"hooks: {calendly: {event_types: [...]}}"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Cal.com"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"The webhook:"},{"s":" Settings > Developer > Webhooks > New. Subscriber URL: the "},{"code":"calcom"},{"s":" hook's address. Triggers: Booking Created, Booking Cancelled, Booking Rescheduled. Secret: the hook's secret."}],[{"b":"The embed:"},{"s":" with the script tag on the page, Skald sees the booking open ("},{"code":"cal_open"},{"s":") and booked ("},{"code":"cal_booked"},{"s":")."}],[{"b":"The visitor ID:"},{"s":" pass it in the embed as "},{"code":"metadata[skv]=skv_..."},{"s":", or as a hidden booking question named "},{"code":"skv"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"Event types:"},{"s":" "},{"b":"Only these Cal.com event types"},{"s":" on the Integrations page takes event type ids ("},{"code":"1234"},{"s":") or slugs ("},{"code":"30min"},{"s":", or the page's address "},{"code":"https://cal.com/example/30min"},{"s":"). Config: "},{"code":"hooks: {calcom_event_types: [...]}"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"A relay of your own"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Some sites want their own filtering, or to add something before Skald sees it. Then the site receives the tool's webhook itself:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Check the tool's signature with the tool's key."}],[{"s":"Keep what you want. Drop the rest, and store nothing of it."}],[{"s":"Sign the kept body again with Skald's "},{"code":"calendly"},{"s":" hook secret, in Calendly's scheme: "},{"code":"Calendly-Webhook-Signature: t=<unix seconds>,v1=<hex HMAC-SHA256 of \"<t>.<body>\">"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Post it to "},{"code":"/traffic-hooks/example.com/calendly"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"For the common case, keeping some event types, the filter above does this for you. You do not need a relay."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"See also "},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":" for every tool, and "},{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"},{"s":" for what started, completed and abandoned mean."}]}]},{"id":"funnels-and-goals","title":"Funnels and goals","summary":[{"s":"How to build a funnel of pages and events, save it and read its history, how goals work on the Events tab, and how to find badly tagged campaign links."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"Funnels"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A funnel answers \"how many visits went through these pages, in this order, and where did the rest leave?\". Open "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Funnels","href":"#sales/funnels"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"How steps are counted"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"A visit reaches a step when it reads a page that matches it, after the step before."}],[{"s":"The page that met one step may also meet the next. So \"Any page\" then \"/pricing/\" counts a visit that landed straight on pricing."}],[{"s":"The page steps are built from each visit's pages in order. These are kept for a few days (7 by default), so a new funnel shows only those days. Save it to count it every day (see \"Funnel history\")."}]]},{"t":"h3","text":"Build a funnel"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each page step has a choice of how it matches pages:"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Choice"}],[{"s":"Matches"}],[{"s":"Example"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Any page"}],[{"s":"every page; as a first step, the visit's start"}],[{"s":"-"}]],[[{"s":"Page is"}],[{"s":"that exact page, with or without the last slash"}],[{"code":"/pricing/"}]],[[{"s":"Starts with"}],[{"s":"every page whose address begins this way"}],[{"code":"/blog/"}]],[[{"s":"Page named"}],[{"s":"a page whose last part is this word, in any language folder"}],[{"code":"pricing"},{"s":" matches "},{"code":"/pricing/"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"/fr/pricing/"}]]]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Funnels","href":"#sales/funnels"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"In "},{"b":"Starting from"},{"s":", choose where the visits came from: "},{"b":"Any source"},{"s":", a kind of source (such as Search engine or AI assistant), or one assistant under "},{"b":"One assistant"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"For each step, choose how it matches pages (above), then type the page."}],[{"s":"To let a step match several pages, type them separated by a vertical bar, such as "},{"code":"/pricing/ | /plans/"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Add a step"},{"s":" for the next one. A funnel has up to 8 steps."}],[{"s":"To remove a step, press the "},{"b":"×"},{"s":" beside it."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The tab suggests pages your visitors read as you type."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Event steps"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A step can also be an event from the "},{"a":"tracking script","href":"#help?part=tracking-script"},{"s":", such as a button click or a demo booked."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Add a step"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"In the step's list, look under "},{"b":"An event, from the beacon"},{"s":" and choose the event."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Event steps are counted as events on the same days, beside the visits. They are never joined to a visit, so they are not a share of the step before. When "},{"b":"Starting from"},{"s":" is a single assistant or site, an event step shows \"not split by this source\"."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Lead steps"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A funnel can also end with steps from your website's lead database: Opened Book a demo, Sign-up, Contact form, Early access, Demo booked. They are counted by the lead's first-touch source, beside the visits, never joined to them. They are counted once the funnel is saved."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Lead steps cannot be added from the step list. The built-in funnel "},{"b":"Landing to lead"},{"s":" has them: landed, pricing, a sign-up or contact page, then demo opened, lead and demo booked."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Read the result"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"The heading says how many visits went through every page step, out of how many started."}],[{"s":"Each step shows its visits and its share of the start."}],[{"s":"Between steps, a line says how many left before this step. A drop of half or more is marked."}]]},{"t":"h3","text":"Open a step's visits"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Click a page step's bar."}],[{"s":"The visits that reached it are listed below, each with its pages in order. Press "},{"b":"Show 20 more"},{"s":" for more."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Left after it"},{"s":" to see the visits that stopped at this step instead. Press "},{"b":"Reached it"},{"s":" to go back."}],[{"s":"Click the bar again to close the list."}]]},{"t":"h3","text":"Save a funnel"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Type a name in "},{"b":"Name this funnel"},{"s":". If you leave it empty, the steps become the name."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Save funnel"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Saved funnels show as buttons above the builder. Click one to open it. Press "},{"b":"×"},{"s":" beside one to delete it. "},{"b":"Landing to lead"},{"s":" is built in and cannot be deleted."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Saved for everyone"},{"s":": your server keeps saved funnels for the whole team."}],[{"b":"Saved on this browser"},{"s":": your server does not keep them, so they live only in this browser (up to 20)."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"With accounts, saved funnels are shared by every site of the install, so only an install admin can save or delete them. Viewers can open them but not change them."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A funnel also lives in the page's address. Copy the link to share a funnel you have not saved."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Funnel history"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A saved funnel is counted every day from the day it is saved, so it covers any date range, not only the days visits are kept. Its first day shows after the next daily run."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The "},{"b":"History"},{"s":" section shows:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"The visits at each step over the date range, and what share of the step before went on."}],[{"b":"Visits at each step, per day"},{"s":": one line per step. The gap between two lines is the visits lost between them."}],[{"b":"By source type"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"By device"},{"s":": each step per source or device, and "},{"b":"Went through"},{"s":" (the last step as a share of the first)."}],[{"b":"Where they went next"},{"s":": for each step, the next page of the visits that went no further, or \"Left the site\"."}],[{"b":"Time to go through"},{"s":": from the first step to the last, from under 10 seconds to 30 minutes or more."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"History counts page steps only. Days before the funnel was saved are \"not recorded\", never zero. A day that did not pass Skald's checks is withheld and left out. No share is given over fewer than 10 visits."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Goals"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A goal is an event from the tracking script that counts as success for you, such as \"Demo booked\" or \"Sign-up sent\". Skald shows each goal per 100 visits, by source."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Where goals are set"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"You need to be an admin of the site."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Events","href":"#sales/events"},{"s":" and select "},{"b":"Edit goals"},{"s":" beside the Goals heading. Or open "},{"b":"Settings > This site > Sites"},{"s":" ("},{"a":"Sites","href":"#settings/sites"},{"s":")."}],[{"s":"In the "},{"b":"Goals"},{"s":" box, tick the events that count as success, such as "},{"b":"Sign-up sent"},{"s":" or "},{"b":"Demo booked"},{"s":". Up to 10."}],[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Save"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The events your site has already counted come first. Events not counted yet are under "},{"b":"Not counted yet"},{"s":", so you can set a goal before the event starts."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Goals show from the next run, for every day already counted. To have no goal, untick them all and save."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"On a server without accounts, there is no Settings page for goals. The person who runs your Skald server names them in the server's settings ("},{"code":"beacon.goals"},{"s":"). A goal saved in the app replaces that list for your site."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Where goals show"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Events","href":"#sales/events"},{"s":" and choose a date range. The "},{"b":"Goals"},{"s":" section has one table per goal:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Source"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Visits"},{"s":" from that source, the goal's events, and "},{"b":"Per 100 visits"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"The heading gives the whole site's rate."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"How to read it:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Visits come from your server log; events come from the tracking script. Two counts side by side, never joined per visit."}],[{"s":"A day counts only when both passed their checks. Today's goals appear after midnight."}],[{"s":"No rate is given over fewer than 10 visits."}],[{"s":"Goals are for the whole site. The page filter does not apply to them."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If no goal is set, the section says so, with a link to set one."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"For conversions from all sources (bookings, payments, CRM deals), with completion rates and sources, use "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Pipeline","href":"#sales/pipeline"},{"s":" with "},{"b":"Count from: Tools"},{"s":". See "},{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"The Events tab"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Leads & sales > Events","href":"#sales/events"},{"s":" shows what people did inside your pages, as totals. Nothing here is tied to a visit or a person. Bots are left out."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"The figures at the top"},{"s":": each kind of event, with its rate per 100 visitors."}],[{"b":"Through the forms"},{"s":": Sign-up started to Sign-up sent, and Demo booking opened to Demo booked, with the share that went on (from five starts)."}],[{"b":"Per day"},{"s":": a line per main event. A hatched stub is a day not counted."}],[{"b":"Goals"},{"s":": see above."}],[{"b":"Which button or form"},{"s":": each event by its name and page, such as a Button click named "},{"code":"pricing_top"},{"s":" on "},{"code":"/pricing/"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"By page"},{"s":" and "},{"b":"By source"},{"s":": one column per kind of event."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Today's events are shown as \"not yet checked\". Events are checked each night against your server log. A day that does not match is left out, and the tab says why. A page marked "},{"b":"flagged"},{"s":" had more events than its page views allow on some day."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Campaign tag problems"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Badly tagged links split one campaign into several, or hide where visitors came from. Skald finds four kinds of problem."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open "},{"a":"Traffic > Sources","href":"#traffic/sources"},{"s":" and scroll to "},{"b":"Campaigns and referrers"},{"s":", then "},{"b":"Tag problems"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Problem"}],[{"s":"What it means"}],[{"s":"How to fix it"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Source tag without a medium"}],[{"s":"the link has "},{"code":"utm_source"},{"s":" but no "},{"code":"utm_medium"},{"s":", so tools cannot tell the channel"}],[{"s":"add "},{"code":"utm_medium"},{"s":", such as "},{"code":"email"},{"s":" or "},{"code":"cpc"}]],[[{"s":"Medium no tool knows"}],[{"code":"utm_medium"},{"s":" is not a usual channel name, so it lands in \"other\""}],[{"s":"use a usual name: "},{"code":"cpc"},{"s":", "},{"code":"email"},{"s":", "},{"code":"social"},{"s":", "},{"code":"referral"}]],[[{"s":"Ad click id without tags"}],[{"s":"an ad click id (such as "},{"code":"gclid"},{"s":" or "},{"code":"fbclid"},{"s":") and no "},{"code":"utm_"},{"s":" tag: the network is known, the campaign is not"}],[{"s":"turn on auto-tagging, or add "},{"code":"utm_campaign"},{"s":" in the ad"}]],[[{"s":"Tags on links between our own pages"}],[{"s":"a "},{"code":"utm_"},{"s":" tag on a link from one of your own pages starts a new source mid-visit"}],[{"s":"never tag links between your own pages"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each problem shows how many visits had it, up to three example landing addresses with their tags, and the pages they landed on. A visit can have more than one problem."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The same section may also list campaigns that appear in your leads but were never seen in your server log. This often means a redirect dropped the tags."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Above it, "},{"b":"UTM tags"},{"s":" lists visits by Source, Medium, Campaign, Term and Content, each with pages per visit, broken links met and form sends."}]}]},{"id":"ai-and-bots","title":"AI & bots: what each crawler costs","summary":[{"s":"See which AI assistants, search engines and bots fetch your site, how much work each one makes for your server, and what one of them did in detail. This guide covers the cost table, the detail view, and what each figure means."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"Where to find it"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"AI & bots"},{"s":". The table "},{"b":"What each crawler costs"},{"s":" is on two tabs:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Crawlers"},{"s":": AI collecting pages for training or AI search, search engines, and bots and scanners."}],[{"b":"Assistants"},{"s":": AI assistants fetching a page because someone asked them a question. Here it is headed "},{"b":"What each assistant costs"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Pick the period at the top as on any other page: today, yesterday, a number of days, or your own dates."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What the columns mean"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Column"}],[{"s":"What it is"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Name"}],[{"s":"The name the crawler gives itself. Bots without a known name go by the name in their user agent. Scanner probes are one row, "},{"b":"(scanner probes)"},{"s":"."}]],[[{"s":"Requests"}],[{"s":"Every request it made in the period."}]],[[{"s":"Bytes sent"}],[{"s":"How much your server sent it, from the size field of each log line."}]],[[{"s":"Mean time"}],[{"s":"How long your server took per request, on average."}]],[[{"s":"p90 time"}],[{"s":"9 in 10 of its requests took no longer than this. Shown for a single day only."}]],[[{"s":"Errors"}],[{"s":"The share of its requests that got an error (4xx or 5xx)."}]],[[{"s":"Distinct paths"}],[{"s":"How many different addresses on your site it asked for."}]],[[{"s":"Re-crawl"}],[{"s":"Requests per distinct path: 3.0× means it fetched each path three times on average."}]],[[{"s":"Last seen"}],[{"s":"Its last request in the period."}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Select a name to open its detail."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"When a figure says \"not recorded\" or \"partial\""},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald only shows what your server log holds. It never fills a gap with zero."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Bytes: not recorded."},{"s":" None of that crawler's log lines had a size. Some log formats and hosting platforms do not write one."}],[{"b":"Bytes: partial."},{"s":" Only some lines had a size. The figure is the sum over those lines; hover over it to see how many."}],[{"b":"Mean time: -"},{"s":" The log does not record how long the server took. nginx does when its log format has "},{"code":"$request_time"},{"s":". Vercel, Caddy and edge records do not."}],[{"b":"p90 time"},{"s":" shows only when the period is a single day. A p90 over many days cannot be built from each day's p90, so for longer periods use the mean, or pick one day."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Figures over several days"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"For a period of more than one day:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Requests, bytes and errors are added up over the days."}],[{"s":"The mean time is weighted by request: a busy day counts more than a quiet one."}],[{"s":"Distinct paths are counted per day and added up. A path fetched on two days counts twice. Re-crawl is therefore requests per path within a day."}],[{"s":"Each day keeps its 50 busiest names per group. The rest are one row, "},{"b":"(all others)"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"The detail view"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Select a name in the table, or any crawler name elsewhere on AI & bots. The detail opens on the right. Under "},{"b":"What it costs and what it fetched"},{"s":" you see:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Requests, bytes sent, mean server time and errors"},{"s":" for the period."}],[{"b":"From an address checked as theirs"},{"s":": the share of its requests from an address that really belongs to its owner. Requests that use a crawler's name from an address that is not theirs are counted apart, as \"claims to be ...\"."}],[{"b":"Requests per day"},{"s":", as a chart."}],[{"b":"Pages it fetched"},{"s":": the pages it asked for most."}],[{"b":"Status mix"},{"s":": how the server answered."}],[{"b":"Countries of its requests"},{"s":": from the log's country field or the GeoIP file."}],[{"b":"User agents it sent"},{"s":": the exact strings, the five most used each day. These are the crawler's own, never a person's. For scanner probes, link previews and browser-like bots the strings are not kept, because they may be a real person's browser."}],[{"b":"Last seen"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Pages, countries and user agents are kept for the last 30 days. For an older period the detail says how many of its days have them. No address is ever shown."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"How the figures are checked"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Every figure here is counted twice, by two pieces of code written apart: the daily count, and an independent recount from the raw log lines. If the two disagree, the day is withheld until someone finds out why. A withheld day is left out of every total and named at the top of the page."}]}]},{"id":"api","title":"The read-only API","summary":[{"s":"Every figure Skald shows is also a JSON file that a script, a spreadsheet or another tool can read with a token. This guide covers tokens, scopes, the addresses to call, and what the answers look like."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"What the API is"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The API gives you the same data files the dashboard itself reads. Nothing is counted again, and nothing can be changed through it. It is read-only."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The files are rewritten every 2 minutes. Each file says when it was written, in its "},{"code":"generated_at"},{"s":" field."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"There are two ways in:"}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Way in"}],[{"s":"Who it is for"}],[{"s":"How it proves who you are"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"While signed in"}],[{"s":"You, in your own browser, for a quick look"}],[{"s":"Your dashboard sign-in"}]],[[{"s":"With a token"}],[{"s":"A script, a spreadsheet, another tool"}],[{"s":"A token in the "},{"code":"Authorization"},{"s":" header"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Both ways show exactly the same files."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Where to find it"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > API & tokens"},{"s":", or go straight to "},{"a":"API & tokens","href":"#settings/api"},{"s":". Settings opens from the gear at the foot of the sidebar."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The page shows:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"the address of the overview file for this site, ready to copy, both for a signed-in browser and for a token;"}],[{"s":"a curl command for each, ready to copy;"}],[{"b":"Files this page serves"},{"s":": every file name you can put in place of "},{"code":"overview"},{"s":";"}],[{"s":"the list of tokens, and the form to make a new one (admins only)."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Tokens"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A token is a long secret that lets a script read your figures without a password. It looks like this:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"skald_<id>_<secret>"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Treat it like a password. Keep it in a password manager or your tool's secret store. Never put it in a shared document, a chat, or a code repository."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Who can make tokens"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Only an owner or an admin of the organisation can make, see or revoke tokens. A viewer sees a note that tokens are for admins. See "},{"a":"Sign-in and team","href":"#help?part=sign-in-and-team"},{"s":" for roles."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Make a token"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > API & tokens"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Make a token"},{"s":", type a "},{"b":"Name"},{"s":" that says what it is for, for example \"Weekly sheet\"."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Sites it may read"},{"s":", tick each site the token may read. At least one is needed."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Scopes"},{"s":", tick what the token may do. "},{"b":"Read"},{"s":" is ticked for you. The scopes are explained below."}],[{"s":"Leave "},{"b":"Private"},{"s":" off unless the script really needs visitor addresses."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Make token"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Copy the token from the green box. It is shown only this once."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"I have copied it"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Skald keeps only a fingerprint of the token, never the token itself. If you lose it, nobody can show it to you again. Revoke it and make a new one."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"The token list"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The list shows each token's "},{"b":"Name"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Sites"},{"s":", "},{"b":"Scopes"},{"s":", when it was "},{"b":"Made"},{"s":" and by whom, and when it was "},{"b":"Last used"},{"s":". The token itself is never shown again."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"How long a token lasts"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A token has no expiry date. It works until one of these happens:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"an admin revokes it;"}],[{"s":"the person who made it is removed, disabled, or is no longer an owner or admin."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The second rule means a token stops at once when its maker leaves the team. Make tokens for long-running jobs with that in mind."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Revoke a token"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > API & tokens"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Find the token in the list and press "},{"b":"Revoke"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Yes, revoke"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Every script using it stops at once. Revoking cannot be undone."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Scopes"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A scope is what a token may do. A token can have more than one."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Scope"}],[{"s":"Label in the app"}],[{"s":"What it allows"}]],"rows":[[[{"code":"read"}],[{"s":"Read"}],[{"s":"Read every figure these pages show, as JSON, through the API"}]],[[{"code":"read_private"}],[{"s":"Read private files"}],[{"s":"Also read the two files that hold visitor addresses, "},{"code":"requests"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"ai_activity"},{"s":", and look a person up"}]],[[{"code":"mcp"}],[{"s":"MCP"}],[{"s":"Let an AI assistant ask about your traffic through the MCP server"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The "},{"b":"Private"},{"s":" box on the form does the same as "},{"b":"Read private files"},{"s":". Ticking either one is enough."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"There is a fourth scope, "},{"code":"ingest"},{"s":". It sends log lines into Skald and reads nothing. You do not make it on this page; it comes with adding a site."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"A token with only "},{"b":"MCP"},{"s":" cannot read the API, and a token with only "},{"b":"Read"},{"s":" cannot be used by an AI assistant. Tick both if one token must do both."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"The addresses to call"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Every address starts with your dashboard's own address. In the examples below it is "},{"code":"https://analytics.example.com"},{"s":", and the site is "},{"code":"example.com"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"With a token:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"https://analytics.example.com/traffic-api/v1/<site>/<file>\nhttps://analytics.example.com/traffic-api/v1/<site>/<view>/<file>"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"While signed in, in your browser:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"https://analytics.example.com/traffic/<site>/api/v1/<file>\nhttps://analytics.example.com/traffic/<site>/<view>/api/v1/<file>"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"code":"<site>"},{"s":" is the site's name, for example "},{"code":"example.com"},{"s":"."}],[{"code":"<view>"},{"s":" is a part of the site, such as "},{"code":"us-english"},{"s":". Leave it out for the whole site."}],[{"code":"<file>"},{"s":" is a file name without "},{"code":".json"},{"s":", for example "},{"code":"overview"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The signed-in address also lists the files a page has: end it at "},{"code":"api/v1/"},{"s":". The token address has no list; use "},{"b":"Files this page serves"},{"s":" on the API & tokens page instead."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"The main files"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"File"}],[{"s":"What it holds"}]],"rows":[[[{"code":"overview"}],[{"s":"Headline figures per day: visits, pages read, AI and search fetches, 404s, errors"}]],[[{"code":"live"}],[{"s":"Today so far, from the 2-minute snapshot"}]],[[{"code":"visits"}],[{"s":"Visits per day, and today's anonymous journeys"}]],[[{"code":"hourly"}],[{"s":"Figures per hour"}]],[[{"code":"breakdowns"}],[{"s":"Countries, sources, devices, browsers and more"}]],[[{"code":"pages"}],[{"s":"Each page: readers, entries, exits, AI and search fetches"}]],[[{"code":"campaigns"}],[{"s":"Tagged links and campaigns"}]],[[{"code":"bots"}],[{"s":"Crawlers and bots"}]],[[{"code":"leads"}],[{"s":"Leads from the website's forms"}]],[[{"code":"conversions"}],[{"s":"Demos, forms, sign-ups and payments by stage"}]],[[{"code":"funnels"}],[{"s":"Saved funnels and their results"}]],[[{"code":"quality"}],[{"s":"Whether each day was read whole and passed its checks"}]],[[{"code":"health"}],[{"s":"Server health"}]],[[{"code":"alerts"}],[{"s":"Open alerts"}]],[[{"code":"ours"}],[{"s":"Your own traffic and the heartbeat"}]],[[{"code":"ai_activity"}],[{"s":"What AI assistants did (holds addresses: needs "},{"b":"Read private files"},{"s":")"}]],[[{"code":"requests"}],[{"s":"The recent request log (holds addresses: needs "},{"b":"Read private files"},{"s":")"}]],[[{"code":"people?q=..."}],[{"s":"One person by IP address, email, visitor ID or lead: their visits, leads and conversions, linked. Needs "},{"b":"Read private files"},{"s":"; each search goes to the audit log"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The API & tokens page lists every file your site really has."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Examples with curl"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Read the overview of the whole site:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer skald_<id>_<secret>\" \\\n  https://analytics.example.com/traffic-api/v1/example.com/overview"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Read the pages of one view:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer skald_<id>_<secret>\" \\\n  https://analytics.example.com/traffic-api/v1/example.com/us-english/pages"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The header must be exactly "},{"code":"Authorization: Bearer "},{"s":" followed by the token."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What an answer looks like"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Every file starts with the same few fields, then its own figures. Most files hold one entry per day for the last 180 days, oldest first. A short piece of "},{"code":"overview"},{"s":":"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"{\"schema_version\": 1, \"generated_at\": \"2026-10-08T07:16:02-04:00\",\n \"site\": \"example.com\", \"view\": null, \"timezone\": \"America/New_York\",\n \"anchor\": \"2026-10-07\", \"first_day\": \"2026-09-01\",\n \"days\": [\n  {\"day\": \"2026-10-05\", \"state\": \"withheld\", \"problems\": \"the audit did not agree\"},\n  {\"day\": \"2026-10-06\", \"state\": \"ok\", \"not_found_people\": null, \"server_errors\": 0,\n   \"visits\": {\"visits\": 120, \"views\": 170, \"one_page\": 98, \"median_seconds\": 4}},\n  {\"day\": \"2026-10-07\", \"state\": \"ok\", \"not_found_people\": 9, \"server_errors\": 0,\n   \"visits\": {\"visits\": 140, \"views\": 190, \"one_page\": 118, \"median_seconds\": 3}}\n ]}"},{"t":"h3","text":"Read the day's state first"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each day has a "},{"code":"state"},{"s":". Check it before you use any figure."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"State"}],[{"s":"Figures?"}],[{"s":"What it means"}]],"rows":[[[{"code":"ok"}],[{"s":"Yes"}],[{"s":"A whole day that passed every check"}]],[[{"code":"partial"}],[{"s":"Yes"}],[{"s":"Checked, but the logs did not cover the whole day. Do not add it to whole days or compare it with them"}]],[[{"code":"withheld"}],[{"s":"No"}],[{"s":"It failed a check, so Skald shows no figures for it. "},{"code":"problems"},{"s":" says why"}]],[[{"code":"missing"}],[{"s":"No"}],[{"s":"Not collected"}]],[[{"code":"before"}],[{"s":"No"}],[{"s":"Before your history starts"}]]]},{"t":"h3","text":"Unknown is null, never 0"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"A figure that was not recorded is "},{"code":"null"},{"s":". It never becomes "},{"code":"0"},{"s":"."}],[{"code":"0"},{"s":" means Skald counted and found none."}],[{"s":"A withheld or missing day has no figures at all. Leave it out of totals and say so; never count it as zero."}],[{"s":"Visits are an upper bound on people, not a count of people. Requests are never people."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"In a spreadsheet, keep "},{"code":"null"},{"s":" as an empty cell. If you turn it into 0, your totals and averages will be wrong."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Errors"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Status"}],[{"s":"Body"}],[{"s":"When"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"200"}],[{"s":"The file"}],[{"s":"All went well"}]],[[{"s":"401"}],[{"code":"{\"ok\": false, \"error\": \"...\"}"}],[{"s":"No token, a wrong or revoked token, a token for another site, a token without "},{"b":"Read"},{"s":", or a private file without "},{"b":"Read private files"}]],[[{"s":"404"}],[{"code":"{\"ok\": false, \"error\": \"no such file\"}"}],[{"s":"The site, view or file does not exist"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The "},{"code":"error"},{"s":" text says which problem it was, for example \"unknown or revoked token\" or \"this token is not for that site\"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Answers are never cached. Ask again for fresh figures; they change every 2 minutes."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Rate limits"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald sets no request limit of its own on the API today, so you will not see a 429 answer from Skald. Whoever runs your server may add one. The files only change every 2 minutes, so asking more often than that gains nothing. Once every few minutes is plenty for a live screen; once a day is enough for a report."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Servers that use one shared login"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Some Skald servers have no team accounts. Everyone signs in with one shared name and password set on the server. On those servers:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"the API & tokens page shows "},{"b":"With your dashboard login"},{"s":" instead of "},{"b":"While you are signed in"},{"s":";"}],[{"s":"tokens are not made on the page. Whoever runs the server makes them with a command, and the page shows that command;"}],[{"s":"the signed-in address also works from curl with "},{"code":"curl -u <your name>"},{"s":", using the dashboard password;"}],[{"s":"the MCP server is not available. See "},{"a":"MCP","href":"#help?part=mcp"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Everything else in this guide is the same."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Related guides"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"a":"MCP","href":"#help?part=mcp"},{"s":": let an AI assistant read your figures."}],[{"a":"Sign-in and team","href":"#help?part=sign-in-and-team"},{"s":": roles, and who may make tokens."}],[{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":": which files hold addresses."}]]}]},{"id":"mcp","title":"Ask an AI assistant about your traffic (MCP)","summary":[{"s":"Connect Claude, ChatGPT or another AI assistant to Skald, so you can ask about your traffic in plain words. This guide covers the address to use, the token it needs, setup for each assistant, and what it can and cannot see."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"What MCP is"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"MCP (Model Context Protocol) is a standard way for an AI assistant to use outside tools, such as Skald."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Once connected, you can ask \"How did last week compare with the week before?\" and the assistant reads the answer from Skald. It does not guess."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Before you start"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"You need three things:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"MCP switched on for your server."},{"s":" Whoever runs your Skald server turns it on. If it is off, the address below answers \"MCP is not switched on here\"."}],[{"b":"Team accounts."},{"s":" MCP works only on servers where people sign in with their own accounts. It is not available on servers with one shared login."}],[{"b":"A token with the MCP scope."},{"s":" Only an owner or admin can make one."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"The address to use"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The MCP address is your dashboard's address, followed by "},{"code":"/traffic-mcp"},{"s":":"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"https://analytics.example.com/traffic-mcp"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Copy yours from "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > API & tokens"},{"s":", under "},{"b":"For an AI assistant (MCP)"},{"s":". The same box has the Claude Code command, ready to copy."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"The address is the same for every site on your server. The token decides which sites the assistant may read."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Make a token for the assistant"},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > API & tokens"},{"s":", or go to "},{"a":"API & tokens","href":"#settings/api"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Make a token"},{"s":", type a "},{"b":"Name"},{"s":", for example \"Claude\"."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Sites it may read"},{"s":", tick the sites the assistant may read."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"Scopes"},{"s":", tick "},{"b":"MCP"},{"s":". You can untick "},{"b":"Read"},{"s":" if this token is only for the assistant."}],[{"s":"Leave "},{"b":"Private"},{"s":" off. With it on, the assistant can see visitor addresses in today's AI activity and look a person up ("},{"code":"find_person"},{"s":": their visits, emails and names). Turn it on only if you truly need that."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Make token"},{"s":" and copy the token. It is shown only once."}],[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"I have copied it"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The token looks like "},{"code":"skald_<id>_<secret>"},{"s":". In every step below, put your own token where you see "},{"code":"skald_<id>_<secret>"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"See "},{"a":"The read-only API","href":"#help?part=api"},{"s":" for more on tokens."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Connect Claude Code"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Run this one command in your terminal:"}]},{"t":"pre","text":"claude mcp add --transport http skald https://analytics.example.com/traffic-mcp \\\n  --header \"Authorization: Bearer skald_<id>_<secret>\""},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Then start Claude Code and type "},{"code":"/mcp"},{"s":" to see that "},{"code":"skald"},{"s":" is connected."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Connect Claude Desktop"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Claude Desktop needs a small helper to send the token, because Skald does not offer a sign-in screen (OAuth) yet. The common helper is "},{"code":"mcp-remote"},{"s":", which needs Node.js on your computer."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"In Claude Desktop, open "},{"b":"Settings > Developer"},{"s":" and press "},{"b":"Edit Config"},{"s":". This opens "},{"code":"claude_desktop_config.json"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Add Skald to it as below, with your own address and token."}],[{"s":"Save the file and restart Claude Desktop."}],[{"s":"Start a new chat and check that the Skald tools are listed."}]]},{"t":"pre","text":"{\n  \"mcpServers\": {\n    \"skald\": {\n      \"command\": \"npx\",\n      \"args\": [\"mcp-remote\", \"https://analytics.example.com/traffic-mcp\",\n               \"--header\", \"Authorization:${SKALD_AUTH}\"],\n      \"env\": {\"SKALD_AUTH\": \"Bearer skald_<id>_<secret>\"}\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Claude's "},{"b":"Connectors"},{"s":" screen (Add custom connector) asks for a URL and, at most, OAuth details. It has no place for a token, so it cannot connect to Skald yet. Use the config file instead."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If you run the Skald server yourself, you can also connect over SSH without a token. The server docs explain how."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Connect ChatGPT"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald does not offer OAuth sign-in yet. ChatGPT can only use Skald where it lets you set the "},{"code":"Authorization"},{"s":" header yourself."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"ChatGPT app (connectors, developer mode):"},{"s":" these screens ask for OAuth or no sign-in. They cannot send the token, so they cannot connect to Skald yet."}],[{"b":"OpenAI API:"},{"s":" a developer can add Skald as a remote MCP server, with the server URL "},{"code":"https://analytics.example.com/traffic-mcp"},{"s":" and the header "},{"code":"Authorization: Bearer skald_<id>_<secret>"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Other MCP clients"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Any MCP client works if it can do both of these:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"connect to a remote server over HTTP (often called \"Streamable HTTP\");"}],[{"s":"send a custom header with every request."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Use the address above and the header "},{"code":"Authorization: Bearer skald_<id>_<secret>"},{"s":". Skald answers each request with plain JSON and does not keep an event stream open."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"The tools it offers"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The assistant chooses these tools itself. Dates are in your site's own time zone. With no dates, a tool uses the last 7 whole days: yesterday and the 6 days before it."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Tool"}],[{"s":"What it answers"}]],"rows":[[[{"code":"list_sites"}],[{"s":"The sites you may read, their views, and the days held"}]],[[{"code":"overview"}],[{"s":"Visits, pages read, AI fetches, search fetches, 404s, server errors, and the change against the period before"}]],[[{"code":"breakdown"}],[{"s":"Visits by country, source, campaign, landing page, device, browser, hour, operating system or referrer"}]],[[{"code":"top_pages"}],[{"s":"The pages people read most, with AI fetches of each"}]],[[{"code":"ai_activity"}],[{"s":"Which AI assistants and crawlers came, what they fetched, and visits that followed an assistant's link"}]],[[{"code":"leads"}],[{"s":"Leads from the website's forms, by type and by first source (totals only)"}]],[[{"code":"funnel"}],[{"s":"A saved funnel, or steps you name, over the last 7 days and today"}]],[[{"code":"compare"}],[{"s":"Two date ranges side by side, up to 400 days"}]],[[{"code":"page_story"}],[{"s":"One page since it was published: first Googlebot, first AI crawler, first person, first lead"}]],[[{"code":"live_today"}],[{"s":"Today so far, from the 2-minute snapshot (partial, never compared)"}]],[[{"code":"data_quality"}],[{"s":"Per day: whether the log was read whole and passed its checks"}]],[[{"code":"site_health"}],[{"s":"Open alerts, heartbeat uptime, errors today, late runs, page speed"}]],[[{"code":"conversions"}],[{"s":"Demos, forms, sign-ups and payments by stage: started, completed, abandoned, won, lost. The completed ones and the leads, by source, first touch, landing page, country, campaign, device or tool"}]],[[{"code":"find_person"}],[{"s":"One person by IP address, email, visitor ID or lead: their visits, leads and conversions. Only with "},{"b":"Private"},{"s":"; each search goes to the audit log"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"It also offers a ready prompt, "},{"b":"weekly_report"},{"s":", which asks the assistant for a short weekly report."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Questions to try"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"\"Which sites can you see in Skald?\""}],[{"s":"\"How did last week compare with the week before?\""}],[{"s":"\"Where did our visits come from in the last 30 days?\""}],[{"s":"\"Which pages did ChatGPT fetch yesterday?\""}],[{"s":"\"What are our ten most-read pages this month?\""}],[{"s":"\"Was any day withheld last week, and why?\""}],[{"s":"\"How is the pricing page doing since it was published?\""}],[{"s":"\"How many demos were booked last month, and from which sources?\""}],[{"s":"\"Is the site healthy right now?\""}],[{"s":"\"Write a short weekly report for example.com.\""}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"How honest the answers are"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald gives the assistant the same rules the dashboard follows:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Visits are called \"visits (an upper bound on people)\". A visit count is at most the number of people, never a count of them."}],[{"s":"Totals use whole, checked days only. Withheld, partial and missing days are named by date and left out. They are never counted as zero."}],[{"s":"A figure that was not recorded is null, never 0."}],[{"s":"A change against an earlier period is given only when both periods are whole."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"If the assistant says a day was withheld, that day failed a check. See "},{"a":"FAQ","href":"#help?part=faq"},{"s":" for what that means."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Safety"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Read-only."},{"s":" Every tool only reads. The assistant cannot change settings, delete data, or add anything."}],[{"b":"Only your sites."},{"s":" The token reads only your organisation's sites, and only the ones you ticked. Every tool checks this again on each call."}],[{"b":"No addresses by default."},{"s":" Without "},{"b":"Private"},{"s":", no answer carries a visitor's address, and the assistant cannot look a person up."}],[{"b":"Turn it off at once."},{"s":" To cut off an assistant, revoke its token: open "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > API & tokens"},{"s":", press "},{"b":"Revoke"},{"s":", then "},{"b":"Yes, revoke"},{"s":". It stops working immediately."}],[{"b":"Tied to the maker."},{"s":" If the person who made the token leaves the team or stops being an admin, the token stops too."}],[{"b":"Keep the token secret."},{"s":" It sits in your assistant's settings. Do not paste it into a chat or a shared file."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"If it does not connect"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"What you see"}],[{"s":"What to check"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"\"MCP is not switched on here\""}],[{"s":"Ask whoever runs your server to switch MCP on"}]],[[{"s":"401, \"Unauthorized\""}],[{"s":"The token is wrong, revoked, or has no "},{"b":"MCP"},{"s":" scope. Make a new one with "},{"b":"MCP"},{"s":" ticked"}]],[[{"s":"\"this token is not for that site\""}],[{"s":"Tick that site when you make the token"}]],[[{"s":"403, \"this Origin may not call the MCP server\""}],[{"s":"You are calling from a web page. Use an assistant app or command line instead"}]],[[{"s":"405"}],[{"s":"The client tried to open an event stream. Pick the HTTP (Streamable HTTP) transport"}]]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Related guides"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"a":"The read-only API","href":"#help?part=api"},{"s":": tokens and scopes in full."}],[{"a":"Sign-in and team","href":"#help?part=sign-in-and-team"},{"s":": who is an admin."}],[{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":": what holds visitor addresses."}]]}]},{"id":"settings-and-retention","title":"Settings and retention","summary":[{"s":"What each settings page does, who may change it, and how long Skald keeps each kind of detail."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"Opening Settings"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Select the gear at the foot of the sidebar, or press "},{"code":"g"},{"s":" then "},{"code":","},{"s":" (comma). The settings menu takes the sidebar's place while a settings page is open."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Settings pages come with accounts. On a server with one shared login, most of these values are set in the server's config file by whoever runs it, and the pages say so."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A page you may not change is shown read-only, with the reason beside each field. Pages your role cannot use are left out of the menu."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"The settings menu"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Group"}],[{"s":"Pages"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"You"}],[{"s":"Your account"}]],[[{"s":"Team & access"}],[{"s":"Team, API & tokens (Users, on a server with one shared login)"}]],[[{"s":"This site"}],[{"s":"Sites, Internal traffic, Data retention, Mail, Integrations"}]],[[{"s":"Organisation"}],[{"s":"Add or remove sites, Security, Audit log, Billing"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"b":"Back to the dashboard"},{"s":", at the top of the settings menu, returns to the page you came from."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"These pages have guides of their own:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Your account and Team: "},{"a":"Sign-in and team","href":"#help?part=sign-in-and-team"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"API & tokens: "},{"a":"API","href":"#help?part=api"},{"s":" and "},{"a":"MCP","href":"#help?part=mcp"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Internal traffic: "},{"a":"Internal traffic","href":"#help?part=internal-traffic"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Integrations: "},{"a":"Tracking script","href":"#help?part=tracking-script"},{"s":" and "},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Who may change what"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"\"Admin\" means an owner or admin of the site's organisation. \"Install admin\" is a flag the server admin gives to a person, for settings that apply to every site on the server."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Page"}],[{"s":"Part"}],[{"s":"Who may change it"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Data retention"}],[{"s":"Detail kept for this site"}],[{"s":"Admin"}]],[[{"s":"Data retention"}],[{"s":"People (IP addresses, names and emails)"}],[{"s":"Admin"}]],[[{"s":"Data retention"}],[{"s":"Backups"}],[{"s":"Install admin"}]],[[{"s":"Mail"}],[{"s":"Reports"}],[{"s":"Admin"}]],[[{"s":"Mail"}],[{"s":"Mail server (SMTP), Google PageSpeed"}],[{"s":"Install admin"}]],[[{"s":"Sites"}],[{"s":"Host names, Views, Time zone"}],[{"s":"Admin"}]],[[{"s":"Sites"}],[{"s":"Log file"}],[{"s":"Install admin"}]],[[{"s":"Sites"}],[{"s":"Goals"}],[{"s":"Admin"}]],[[{"s":"Integrations"}],[{"s":"Hooks, event types, outgoing webhooks"}],[{"s":"Admin"}]],[[{"s":"Security"}],[{"s":"Sign-in rules"}],[{"s":"Owner"}]],[[{"s":"Audit log"}],[{"s":"(read only)"}],[{"s":"Admins may read it"}]],[[{"s":"AI & bots > Crawler rules"}],[{"s":"Every crawler"}],[{"s":"Install admin"}]],[[{"s":"Add or remove sites"}],[{"s":"Add a site"}],[{"s":"Admin"}]],[[{"s":"Add or remove sites"}],[{"s":"Remove a site"}],[{"s":"Owner"}]],[[{"s":"Billing"}],[{"s":"Plan and payment"}],[{"s":"Owner"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Viewers see the pages read-only."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Data retention"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Data retention","href":"#settings/retention"},{"s":" sets how long the detail is kept. Totals, page milestones and every stored day's figures are kept forever. They are not a setting."}]},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"Setting"}],[{"s":"What it keeps"}],[{"s":"Range"}],[{"s":"Default"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Detail days"}],[{"s":"Each visit by its labels, and each page's daily figures (used by Compare with… and the page story)"}],[{"s":"30 to 3650 days"}],[{"s":"400"}]],[[{"s":"Journeys"}],[{"s":"Anonymous visits: start time, country, device, source, pages in order"}],[{"s":"1 to 90 days"}],[{"s":"7"}]],[[{"s":"Returning-visitor matching"}],[{"s":"How long a visitor can be recognised as returning"}],[{"s":"1 to 90 days"}],[{"s":"30"}]],[[{"s":"In-page events"}],[{"s":"Events from the script tag"}],[{"s":"30 to 3650 days"}],[{"s":"400"}]],[[{"s":"Visits with addresses"}],[{"s":"Each visit with its IP address and browser (card "},{"b":"People"},{"s":")"}],[{"s":"1 to 3650 days"}],[{"s":"395"}]],[[{"s":"Daily backup copies"}],[{"s":"Copies of the history on the server, for every site"}],[{"s":"1 to 60"}],[{"s":"14"}]],[[{"s":"Weekly backup copies"}],[{"s":"Weekly copies of the history"}],[{"s":"0 to 52"}],[{"s":"8"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each field says where its value comes from: this site, the organisation, the whole server, the config file, or the default."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"People"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The "},{"b":"People"},{"s":" card says what Skald keeps about the people who visit:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Keep visitors' IP addresses"},{"s":": each visit is kept with its IP address, browser, times, pages in order, source, referrer, campaign, country and device. Admins can then look a person up with the search at the top. Off: no address is kept, and the visits already kept with one are deleted at the next nightly run."}],[{"b":"Visits with addresses"},{"s":": how many days those visits are kept. The default is 395."}],[{"b":"Leads' names and emails"},{"s":": "},{"b":"full"},{"s":" keeps a lead's name and email with its conversions; "},{"b":"anonymous"},{"s":" keeps neither."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A new install keeps both. An install that was upgraded from a version before 2.4.0 keeps neither until you turn them on. The field then says \"kept off by the upgrade to 2.4.0\". Your privacy notice must say what you keep before you turn them on. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Keeping less"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Making a window shorter removes stored data, so Skald asks first."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Type the new, smaller number and select "},{"b":"Save"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"The page shows what will go: how many rows and days."}],[{"s":"Type the site's name to confirm, then select "},{"b":"Yes, keep less"},{"s":". Or select "},{"b":"Keep it as it is"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Nothing is removed at once. Removal happens at the next daily run."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A change to "},{"b":"Returning-visitor matching"},{"s":" also changes who counts as a returning visitor from then on."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"If your server sells plans, your plan may cap the detail you can keep. The page then says \"Capped by your plan\"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Mail"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Mail","href":"#settings/mail"},{"s":" sets the mails Skald sends."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Reports"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Daily mail"},{"s":": sent after each morning's run."}],[{"b":"Weekly mail"},{"s":": sent on Mondays."}],[{"b":"Recipients"},{"s":": up to 20 email addresses."}],[{"b":"From name"},{"s":": the name the mail comes from."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each new recipient first gets one mail with a confirm link. They get nothing else until they open the link and select the button on that page. The link works once, for 7 days. Until at least one address is confirmed, the reports are held back, not failed."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The mails carry figures only, never an address and never a journey. A mail that would include a withheld or partial day is held back."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Mail server (SMTP)"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"For install admins. The sender address, server, port, security, user and password apply to every site on the server. The password is write-only: the page only says whether it is set."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Google PageSpeed"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A free API key raises Google's daily limit for the tests on "},{"a":"Site > Speed","href":"#site/speed"},{"s":". It is write-only too."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Send a test mail"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Owners, admins and install admins can send a short test mail through the settings above."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Type the address in "},{"b":"Send to"},{"s":". It must be your own address or a confirmed recipient."}],[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Send test mail"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"At most 3 test mails in 10 minutes."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Alerts and failure mail"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Alerts always show on "},{"a":"Site > Alerts","href":"#site/alerts"},{"s":" and on the bell in the top bar. Alert mails are sent only if the server admin has turned them on. They go to confirmed recipients only."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If the morning run fails, the server can send one short failure mail. It goes to the same people as the daily mail: the confirmed recipients on this page, or the server's own list when none is set here or none has confirmed yet. It uses the mail server set on this page or on the server. A day held back because it did not add up is not a failure, so it sends no failure mail."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Sites"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Sites","href":"#settings/sites"},{"s":" says what counts as this site, and where its log is."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Host names"},{"s":": the names this site answers to, such as "},{"code":"www.example.com"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"example.com"},{"s":". 1 to 50."}],[{"b":"Views"},{"s":": page groups, one per line: a name, the path it starts with, and any paths to leave out. Up to 20. They show in the "},{"b":"Page group"},{"s":" list in the top bar."}],[{"b":"Time zone"},{"s":": the site's own zone. Days are counted midnight to midnight in it."}],[{"b":"Log file"},{"s":": the log folder and file name. For install admins."}],[{"b":"Goals"},{"s":": the page events that count as this site's goals, such as Sign-up sent or Demo booked. Tick up to 10. The events your site has already counted are listed first; the others are under "},{"b":"Not counted yet"},{"s":". See "},{"a":"Funnels and goals","href":"#help?part=funnels-and-goals"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Changes apply from the next run. Days already stored are not counted again."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Logo"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each site shows its own logo: on the page where you choose a site, in the menu's site button, in the site switcher and on the browser tab. The card shows it at those three sizes, and what Skald found on the site."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Choose where it comes from:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"From the site (automatic)"},{"s":": Skald asks your site itself for its app icon, then its favicon. It never asks an outside icon service. It asks again once a week. "},{"b":"Check the site again now"},{"s":" asks at once."}],[{"b":"Upload my own"},{"s":": a PNG, SVG or ICO file, square, at least 64 x 64 pixels, at most 256 KB. An SVG that could run a script or load something from elsewhere is refused; save it again as a plain drawing, or upload a PNG."}],[{"b":"A letter on a colour"},{"s":": the site's first letter on one of four colours. Skald also shows this while there is no logo."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Press "},{"b":"Save"},{"s":". Owners and admins can change the logo; everyone else sees it."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Add or remove sites"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Add or remove sites","href":"#settings/sitesadmin"},{"s":" lists your organisation's sites. If your server offers it, an admin can add a site here. A new site gets a page at once, with a short \"Getting ready\" note until its first figures arrive."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Only an owner can remove a site. A removed site stops being processed. Its data is kept until the server admin deletes it."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Crawler rules"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The rules for AI crawlers are not in Settings any more. They are on "},{"a":"AI & bots > Crawler rules","href":"#ai/rules"},{"s":", next to the crawlers they apply to. Old links to Settings > AI crawlers open that tab."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Crawler rules lets each AI company's crawlers in, or keeps them out. If your server offers it, each company has three choices:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Allow"},{"s":": every crawler of that company may read the site."}],[{"b":"Block training only"},{"s":": crawlers that collect for training are kept out. AI search and answers to people's questions still reach the site."}],[{"b":"Block"},{"s":": every crawler of that company is kept out."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each crawler can also be set on its own: "},{"b":"As"},{"s":" the company, "},{"b":"Always allow"},{"s":" or "},{"b":"Always block"},{"s":". Beside each one is how often it was refused in the last 30 days."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Save"},{"s":". The tab says \"Saved. Being applied to the site...\" and then \"Live on the site\" within a few seconds. "},{"b":"Undo changes"},{"s":" puts back what was saved before."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A blocked crawler gets a refusal before the page is served. Some crawlers cannot be told apart by the server: they are marked \"robots.txt only\", and only a line in your robots.txt can ask them to stay away. The tab suggests the lines to use, with a "},{"b":"Copy"},{"s":" button. Under the rules, your site's robots.txt is shown beside each crawler. Skald never writes your robots.txt."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"These rules apply to every site on the server, so only an install admin may change them."}]},{"t":"h3","text":"Suggested llms.txt"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"AI & bots > llms.txt","href":"#ai/llms"},{"s":" shows "},{"b":"Suggested llms.txt"},{"s":": a file you can publish at "},{"code":"/llms.txt"},{"s":" on your site. It follows the format at llmstxt.org: your site's name, a one-line summary, then links to your pages, grouped by section, so an AI assistant knows which pages matter."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald picks the pages people and AI assistants read most over the last 90 days. Only recorded days count; any day left out is named. It leaves out private pages (sign-in, account, cart, search, admin), pages your robots.txt keeps crawlers from, redirects, and pages that are gone. With your website's page list, each link has the page's title; without it, the link is named by its path."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Write the summary line yourself and check the links. Then select "},{"b":"Copy"},{"s":" or "},{"b":"Download"},{"s":" and publish it on your site. Skald never writes it to your website. Your server admin can also print it with "},{"code":"skald llms-txt"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Security"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Security","href":"#settings/security"},{"s":" sets sign-in rules for everyone in the organisation. Only an owner may change them."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Require two-step sign-in"},{"s":": members without it set it up the next time they sign in. Turn it on for your own account first."}],[{"b":"Session length"},{"s":": how long a sign-in lasts at most, 1 to 90 days. The default is 14."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Audit log"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Audit log","href":"#settings/audit"},{"s":" shows who changed what, and when, newest first: settings, the team, tokens, sign-ins and failed sign-ins. Admins may read it. Viewers cannot."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Pick one kind of change in "},{"b":"Action"},{"s":", or keep "},{"b":"Every action"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Download CSV"},{"s":" to keep a copy."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"No password, token, link or address is ever written to the log. Each person search is written too ("},{"code":"people.search"},{"s":"): what kind of value was searched and a one-way code of it, never the value. So is each conversion marked test or not ("},{"code":"conversions.test"},{"s":", "},{"code":"conversions.untest"},{"s":"). Install admins see every organisation's rows."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Billing"},{"t":"p","in":[{"a":"Billing","href":"#settings/billing"},{"s":" shows only on servers that sell plans, and only to owners. Other servers say \"This server does not sell plans.\""}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Your plan"},{"s":": its name, status and trial days left."}],[{"s":"A table of use against the plan's limits: sites, requests this month, members and days of detail kept."}],[{"b":"Plans"},{"s":": select "},{"b":"Choose"},{"s":" and a plan's name to buy it."}],[{"b":"Manage billing"},{"s":": card, invoices and cancelling, on the payment provider's own page."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"\"Requests this month\" counts every request the server logged for your sites, people and machines alike."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If your organisation goes over a limit, every page shows a banner. Nothing is deleted. If a payment is overdue, the organisation becomes read-only: you can still read every page, change your own account and pay, but not change settings or the team."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Related guides"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"a":"Getting started","href":"#help?part=getting-started"}],[{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"}],[{"a":"FAQ","href":"#help?part=faq"}]]}]},{"id":"privacy","title":"Privacy","summary":[{"s":"What Skald keeps about the people who visit, who can see it, for how long, and how a person is removed when they ask."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"The short version"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Skald can keep each visit with its IP address, so you can look a person up and follow them across days. That is a switch, on by default for a new install."}],[{"s":"It can keep the name and email of each lead with its conversions. Also a switch, on by default for a new install."}],[{"s":"An install upgraded from before version 2.4.0 keeps neither until you turn them on."}],[{"s":"Only owners and admins can look a person up. Every search is written to the audit log."}],[{"s":"Stored history (the totals) never holds an address."}],[{"s":"Nothing is hidden: spam, duplicate and test leads, and cancelled, removed and test conversions, are listed, not only counted."}],[{"s":"One command on the server removes a person everywhere Skald keeps them."}]]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Your privacy notice must say what you keep before you turn these on. Some places also need the visitor's consent."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What is kept about a visit"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"When "},{"b":"Keep visitors' IP addresses"},{"s":" is on ("},{"b":"Settings > Data retention > People"},{"s":"), each visit is kept with:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"its IP address and browser string"}],[{"s":"when it started and ended"}],[{"s":"the pages it read, in order"}],[{"s":"where it came from: source, referring site, campaign"}],[{"s":"its country and device"}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A visit here is a visit that read at least one page, the same visit Traffic > Visitors counts. Visits are kept for 395 days by default ("},{"b":"Visits with addresses"},{"s":"). Turn the switch off and no address is kept from then on. The visits already kept with an address are deleted at the next nightly run."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"These visits are kept apart from the history, in the conversions file on your server. They are counted twice like everything else: each morning Skald counts every address's visits again from the raw log, by separate code. A day that does not match is withheld."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What is kept about a lead"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"When "},{"b":"Leads' names and emails"},{"s":" is "},{"b":"full"},{"s":", the name and email of each lead are kept with its conversions. With "},{"b":"anonymous"},{"s":", neither is kept."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald reads your website's lead database without changing it. Leads marked spam or duplicate there, and leads marked test, are left out of every figure. They are listed in full: on "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Pipeline","href":"#sales/pipeline"},{"s":", turn on "},{"b":"Show left out"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Looking a person up"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Owners and admins see a "},{"b":"Find a person"},{"s":" box at the top of every page; on a narrower screen it is a search icon. The same search is on "},{"a":"Leads & sales > People","href":"#sales/people"},{"s":", and "},{"b":"Ctrl K"},{"s":" (or "},{"b":"Cmd K"},{"s":") also offers "},{"b":"Find a person"},{"s":". Type one of these:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"an IP address"}],[{"s":"an email"}],[{"s":"a lead's number or reference"}],[{"s":"a visitor ID ("},{"code":"skv_..."},{"s":")"}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The person opens in a panel on the right:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Linked"},{"s":": the IP addresses, emails, visitor IDs and leads tied to them, and what this site keeps."}],[{"b":"Visits"},{"s":": every visit kept with that address, with its pages in order, source, referring site, country and device. A day whose figures did not add up is marked \"withheld day\"."}],[{"b":"Requests in the last 6 hours"},{"s":": the address's requests from Site > Requests."}],[{"b":"Leads"},{"s":": their leads, spam and test ones too."}],[{"b":"Leads and the visits that sent a form at their time"},{"s":": visits that sent a form from 2 minutes before a lead to 30 seconds after it. This is a match by time only. It is likely the same person, never certain: the lead database keeps no address."}],[{"b":"Conversions"},{"s":": every conversion, cancelled and test ones too, and the rows removed by a sync."}],[{"b":"Pages seen by its visitor IDs"},{"s":", when the site has visitor IDs on."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Every address, email, lead and visitor ID in the panel is a link. Select it to open that one."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Each search is written to the "},{"a":"audit log","href":"#settings/audit"},{"s":": who searched, when, and what kind of value. Never the value itself."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Viewers cannot look a person up. An API token or an AI assistant can, only with the "},{"b":"Read private files"},{"s":" scope. See "},{"a":"API","href":"#help?part=api"},{"s":" and "},{"a":"MCP","href":"#help?part=mcp"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Where addresses appear"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Addresses show only behind sign-in:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"The person search, for owners and admins."}],[{"a":"Site > Requests","href":"#site/requests"},{"s":": the last 6 hours of the request log."}],[{"s":"Today's AI activity, on "},{"a":"AI & bots > Assistants","href":"#ai/assistants"},{"s":" when the period is Today (or "},{"b":"Today · Live"},{"s":" is on): today only."}],[{"s":"The internal-address list in "},{"a":"Internal traffic","href":"#settings/internal"},{"s":", so your team can manage it."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"They never appear in a stored day's totals, a CSV export of history, or a mail."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"How long things are kept"},{"t":"table","head":[[{"s":"What"}],[{"s":"Kept"}]],"rows":[[[{"s":"Raw access logs, with addresses"}],[{"s":"14 days on your server"}]],[[{"s":"Each visit with its address (when kept)"}],[{"s":"395 days, or what you set"}]],[[{"s":"Leads' names and emails (when kept)"}],[{"s":"As long as their conversions: 400 days"}]],[[{"s":"Conversions removed by a sync, whole"}],[{"s":"400 days"}]],[[{"s":"The Requests list, with addresses"}],[{"s":"Its 6-hour window"}]],[[{"s":"Today's AI activity, with addresses"}],[{"s":"Today only"}]],[[{"s":"Returning-visitor codes"}],[{"s":"30 days"}]],[[{"s":"Anonymous journeys"}],[{"s":"7 days"}]],[[{"s":"Per-visit and per-page detail"}],[{"s":"400 days"}]],[[{"s":"In-page events from the script tag"}],[{"s":"400 days"}]],[[{"s":"Totals and labels"}],[{"s":"For good"}]],[[{"s":"Backups of the history and the conversions file (the conversions file holds the kept visits, names and emails)"}],[{"s":"14 daily and 8 weekly copies"}]]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Admins can change most of these. See "},{"a":"Settings and retention","href":"#help?part=settings-and-retention"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Turning it on after an upgrade"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"An install that ran a version before 2.4.0 keeps working as before: no address and no email is kept. The "},{"b":"People"},{"s":" card says \"kept off by the upgrade to 2.4.0\". To turn them on:"}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Change your privacy notice first, so it says what Skald keeps."}],[{"s":"Open "},{"b":"Settings > Data retention"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Under "},{"b":"People"},{"s":", tick "},{"b":"Keep visitors' IP addresses"},{"s":", and set "},{"b":"Leads' names and emails"},{"s":" to "},{"b":"full"},{"s":"."}],[{"s":"Select "},{"b":"Save"},{"s":". It applies from the next run."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"On a server without the Settings pages, the server admin sets "},{"code":"privacy: keep_ips: true"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"conversions: identity: full"},{"s":" in the config file. With Docker, "},{"code":"SKALD_KEEP_IPS=1"},{"s":" and "},{"code":"SKALD_IDENTITY=full"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"The script tag"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The optional "},{"code":"skald.js"},{"s":" tag counts what happens inside a page. It is served from your own site and posts to your own site. No third-party code. See "},{"a":"Tracking script","href":"#help?part=tracking-script"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"No cookie by default."},{"s":" A cookie is set only if your site turns on visitor IDs and also asks to share them across subdomains."}],[{"b":"Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control are respected."},{"s":" A browser that sends either is not counted at all: no ID, no storage, no event."}],[{"b":"Consent first, if you need it."},{"s":" The tag can wait and send nothing until your consent banner says yes. When a visitor says no, the ID and anything stored are deleted."}],[{"b":"Never a field's value."},{"s":" Form events say which form was used, never what was typed. A click on a phone or email link never keeps the number or the address."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Visitor IDs are off by default, and set per site. With them on, the browser keeps a random ID. Turn them on for a site only when that site's privacy notice says so, and let its consent banner gate the tag where consent is needed."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Webhooks and conversions"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"When a booking, form or payment tool sends Skald a webhook, Skald keeps only the fields it needs. Everything else is dropped before anything is written."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Always dropped:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"addresses and browser strings"}],[{"s":"phone numbers"}],[{"s":"answers to form questions and any free text"}],[{"s":"cancel and reschedule links"}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Kept: the action (for example, a demo or a sign-up), its stage, the time, the tool, the tool's own reference, and the source, campaign, landing page, country and device. The name and email too, when "},{"b":"Leads' names and emails"},{"s":" is "},{"b":"full"},{"s":". Skald's outgoing webhooks never send a name or an email."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"See "},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":" and "},{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Removing a person on request"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"If someone asks you to delete their data, the server admin removes it. It cannot be done from the dashboard. Use the search first to see what is kept about them."}]},{"t":"ol","items":[[{"s":"Ask the person for their IP address or email (or a lead's reference)."}],[{"s":"Send it to the person who runs your Skald server."}],[{"s":"The server admin runs "},{"code":"skald forget"},{"s":", first with "},{"code":"--dry-run"},{"s":" to see what it would remove."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"code":"skald forget --ip"},{"s":" with the address:"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Deletes every visit kept with that address."}],[{"s":"Replaces it with \"(removed)\" in the Requests list and today's AI activity."}],[{"s":"Deletes its returning-visitor codes."}],[{"s":"Keeps it hidden for 15 days, longer than the raw logs last. Visits in that time are kept without the address."}],[{"s":"Writes a line to a private log with the counts, never the address."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"code":"skald forget --email"},{"s":" (or "},{"code":"--lead"},{"s":", "},{"code":"--vid"},{"s":") deletes that person's conversions, the rows removed by a sync, their name and email, and the page views of their visitor IDs."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The raw access logs rotate away after 14 days. The server admin can also scrub the address from them sooner. The lead itself, in your website's own database, is yours to delete there."}]},{"t":"quote","in":[{"s":"Backups made before the request still hold what was kept then: the 30-day codes, and the copies of the conversions file, with the visits kept with addresses and the names and emails. They stay on your server, readable only by Skald, and age out on their own (14 daily and 8 weekly copies)."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Related guides"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"a":"Settings and retention","href":"#help?part=settings-and-retention"}],[{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"}],[{"a":"Internal traffic","href":"#help?part=internal-traffic"}],[{"a":"FAQ","href":"#help?part=faq"}]]}]},{"id":"faq","title":"FAQ","summary":[{"s":"Short answers to the questions people ask most about Skald's figures, privacy and data."}],"blocks":[{"t":"h2","text":"Why do my numbers differ from Google Analytics?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"They count different things, in different ways."}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"s":"Google Analytics counts only browsers that run its script and accept it. Ad blockers, privacy browsers and refused consent banners hide many visits from it. Skald reads the server's own log, so it sees those visits."}],[{"s":"Google Analytics cannot see AI assistants, search engines or bots. Skald counts them, but in their own groups, never as people."}],[{"s":"Skald is careful about who is a person: when in doubt, a request is not a person. Its people figure is an upper bound."}],[{"s":"On sites that change pages without loading a new one, the log sees fewer page views than a script does. Skald says so where it matters."}],[{"s":"Days may be cut at different times if the two tools use different time zones."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Why does a day say withheld?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Every figure is counted twice, by two separate roads. If the two counts do not agree, the day is withheld rather than shown wrong. It is never shown as zero. The server admin can see why on "},{"a":"Site > Data quality","href":"#site/quality"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Why is a figure blank and not zero?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Blank means not known. Zero means Skald counted and found nothing. A figure that was not recorded, for example a breakdown from before Skald began collecting it, stays blank. Unknown stays unknown."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Why do my countries say Unknown?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Skald takes a visit's country from your server's log. Some logs carry it (Cloudflare's country, or nginx's own "},{"code":"cc="},{"s":" field). Others do not, for example Caddy's log or nginx's stock log. For those, whoever runs your Skald server can set a GeoIP country file ("},{"code":"logs.country_db"},{"s":", or "},{"code":"SKALD_COUNTRY_DB"},{"s":" in Docker; DB-IP's free file works). Skald then looks up each visit's address in it. Without a file, the country stays Unknown. It is never guessed. See "},{"a":"Docker: first install","href":"#help?part=docker-first-install"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Is AI traffic counted as people?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"No. AI crawlers and fetches are machines, and show under AI & bots ("},{"a":"Assistants","href":"#ai/assistants"},{"s":" and "},{"a":"Crawlers","href":"#ai/crawlers"},{"s":") in their own units. A person who clicks a link in an AI answer is a person, and the AI assistant is shown as their source on "},{"a":"Traffic > Sources","href":"#traffic/sources"},{"s":", and in full on AI & bots > Assistants."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What does \"likely from ChatGPT\" mean?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"It is an estimate, not a count. A person who clicks a link in an AI answer often arrives with no referrer, so the visit shows as Direct. But when they asked, the assistant fetched your page from your server. When a direct visit with no campaign tag lands on a page an assistant fetched in the same minute or up to 15 minutes before, Skald says the visit was "},{"i":"likely"},{"s":" sent by that assistant. It shows these on "},{"a":"AI & bots > Assistants","href":"#ai/assistants"},{"s":", on "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Pipeline","href":"#sales/pipeline"},{"s":" (with either Count from) and in a visitor's details, always marked \"likely\" with an (i) that says how. They are never added to the AI assistant source or to any other figure. See "},{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What did the AI read before it sent this visitor?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Open a visit on "},{"a":"Traffic > Visitors","href":"#traffic/visitors"},{"s":". If the visit followed a link in an AI answer (ChatGPT, Perplexity, Claude, Gemini, Copilot, Mistral, Meta AI), or is likely from one, "},{"b":"What the AI read before this visit"},{"s":" lists the pages that assistant's user fetcher fetched in the 15 minutes before the visit: \"Fetched by ChatGPT in the 15 minutes before\", nearest first, at most 10 pages, with the page the visit landed on marked. It is context, not a count of people: a fetch can be for someone else. Training crawlers (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, ...) are never listed: nobody was waiting on them."}]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"On "},{"a":"AI & bots > Assistants","href":"#ai/assistants"},{"s":", "},{"b":"What the AI read before it sent a visitor"},{"s":" shows, per assistant, the visits from its answers, how many came after it fetched pages, and how many landed on a page it had just fetched (fetch, then a visit to the same page). Likely visits are shown apart: they always land on a page the assistant fetched, because that is how they are inferred. Assistants with no known user fetcher (You.com, Phind, Poe) are not in that table. Days before this feature read \"not recorded\". The window is the same setting as for \"likely\" ("},{"code":"attribution.ai_window_minutes"},{"s":")."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What are the AI alerts?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Three alerts watch how AI assistants treat your site. They show on "},{"a":"Site > Alerts","href":"#site/alerts"},{"s":" (press "},{"b":"AI"},{"s":" to see only them) and in "},{"b":"AI reading changes"},{"s":" on "},{"a":"AI & bots > Assistants","href":"#ai/assistants"},{"s":":"}]},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"AI started reading"},{"s":": an assistant fetched a page yesterday that it had not fetched in the 28 days before."}],[{"b":"AI stopped reading"},{"s":": an assistant that fetched a page in at least 3 of the 4 weeks before has not fetched it for 7 days."}],[{"b":"AI sending people"},{"s":": the visits likely sent by an assistant jumped (3 times its 28-day average, and at least 10) or vanished. With fewer visits Skald says \"too few to judge\" and does not alert."}]]},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"An assistant means its company: GPTBot, OAI-SearchBot and ChatGPT-User are all OpenAI. Each alert names the assistant, the page, the days and the numbers. They use whole days only, and only figures Skald has already counted twice. If a day in the window is withheld or missing, the alert waits; it never fires on a day it cannot trust. The server admin can change the thresholds or switch each one off ("},{"code":"alerts.ai_*"},{"s":" in the server's config). If alert mail is on, the weekly mail lists the week's changes, and an outgoing webhook can receive each one as "},{"code":"ai.reading_changed"},{"s":" ("},{"a":"Webhooks","href":"#help?part=webhooks"},{"s":")."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What do AI assistants and crawlers fetch?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"b":"What they fetch"},{"s":" on "},{"a":"AI & bots > Assistants","href":"#ai/assistants"},{"s":" (fetches for a question) and "},{"a":"Crawlers","href":"#ai/crawlers"},{"s":" (fetches for training) splits every AI fetch by what its address names: a page, your llms.txt ("},{"code":"/llms.txt"},{"s":" or "},{"code":"/llms-full.txt"},{"s":"), a Markdown file ("},{"code":".md"},{"s":"), another text file, robots.txt, a sitemap, or another file (images, scripts, feeds, PDFs). A second table gives the same split per assistant or crawler; each day keeps the 20 with the most fetches and sums the rest in \"(all others)\". The address decides, not the answer: a fetch of an llms.txt you do not have still counts as llms.txt. Days counted before version 2.10.0 have no split, and a range that holds one shows none."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Can Skald see Google's AI Mode?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Only when Google says so. A click from Google whose address carries "},{"code":"udm=50"},{"s":" (Google's AI Mode) is still a search engine visit, but its referring site reads "},{"b":"google.com (AI Mode)"},{"s":" on "},{"a":"Traffic > Sources","href":"#traffic/sources"},{"s":", so you can see it apart. Most clicks from AI Mode and AI Overviews arrive as a plain "},{"code":"google.com"},{"s":", the same as any search click; Skald never guesses which those were."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Can Skald write an llms.txt for my site?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"It suggests one; it never writes it to your website. Open "},{"a":"AI & bots > llms.txt","href":"#ai/llms"},{"s":" and see "},{"b":"Suggested llms.txt"},{"s":": links to the pages people and AI assistants read most over the last 90 days, grouped by section, in the llmstxt.org format. Write the one-line summary yourself, check the links, then copy or download it and publish it at "},{"code":"/llms.txt"},{"s":". See "},{"a":"Settings and retention","href":"#help?part=settings-and-retention"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Why is my own visit not counted?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Your team's addresses are probably listed as internal. Visits from them go to the \"Our own\" group, kept apart from people, so your own testing does not inflate the figures. See "},{"a":"Internal traffic","href":"#help?part=internal-traffic"},{"s":" and "},{"a":"Internal traffic settings","href":"#settings/internal"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Does Skald use cookies?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Not to count visits. Skald reads the server's log, which needs nothing in the browser. The optional script tag sets no cookie by default; a cookie is used only if your site turns on anonymous visitor IDs shared across subdomains. Signing in to the dashboard uses one cookie, for your own session. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"How fresh is today?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Today's figures are recounted about every two minutes. The foot of every page says when they were last updated and when the next update is due. If your server allows it, "},{"b":"Refresh"},{"s":" in the top bar recounts at once. Yesterday becomes a whole, checked day after the morning's run."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Why does a whole day appear only the next morning?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The daily run checks each finished day by both counts before it is stored. Until then, today's figures are a live count, and can change."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Where are my leads?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"On "},{"a":"Leads & sales > Pipeline","href":"#sales/pipeline"},{"s":": leads per day by kind, at which stage, and where they first and last came from. It counts from your lead database by default; switch "},{"b":"Count from"},{"s":" to "},{"b":"Tools"},{"s":" for bookings, forms and payments from your tools. Leads and demos booked also show beside the visitors on Overview > Summary, Traffic > Sources, Pages and Places & devices, and Overview > Insights. Spam, duplicate and test leads are listed with "},{"b":"Show left out"},{"s":". Owners and admins can find one lead, with its email and the visits around it, on "},{"a":"Leads & sales > People","href":"#sales/people"},{"s":" or with the search at the top, when your site keeps names and emails. See "},{"a":"Leads and conversions","href":"#help?part=leads-and-conversions"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"How do I get data out?"},{"t":"ul","items":[[{"b":"Export"},{"s":" in the top bar: every table on the tab as CSV files in a ZIP, the tab as JSON, a printable report, or the report builder for several tabs at once."}],[{"b":"API"},{"s":": every figure as JSON, for a script. Tokens are made in "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > API & tokens"},{"s":". See "},{"a":"API","href":"#help?part=api"},{"s":"."}],[{"b":"MCP"},{"s":": let an AI assistant read your figures. See "},{"a":"MCP","href":"#help?part=mcp"},{"s":"."}]]},{"t":"h2","text":"Who can see visitor addresses?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Only people signed in to your organisation: "},{"a":"Site > Requests","href":"#site/requests"},{"s":" (the last 6 hours), today's AI activity (on AI & bots > Assistants, when the period is Today), and the internal-address list (admins). When your site keeps IP addresses, owners and admins also see each kept visit's address in the person search; every search goes to the audit log. Stored history never holds an address. API tokens see addresses only with the private scope. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"How do I delete someone's data on request?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Send the address or the email address to the person who runs your Skald server. They run Skald's forget command, which deletes the visits, conversions, name and email kept for it. See "},{"a":"Privacy","href":"#help?part=privacy"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Why are my filters greyed out?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"The log keeps each breakdown on its own, so some tabs cannot apply some filters, and filters cannot be crossed (for example, Canada AND Chrome). A greyed-out filter chip is one the tab cannot apply. The tab says which."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"Can I see times in my own time zone?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Yes. Select the round "},{"b":"You"},{"s":" button at the foot of the sidebar and choose "},{"b":"Time zone"},{"s":": your own, the site's, or UTC. Days are still counted midnight to midnight in the site's own zone."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"How do I invite a colleague?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Admins and owners go to "},{"b":"Settings > Team & access > Team"},{"s":" and use "},{"b":"Invite someone"},{"s":". See "},{"a":"Sign-in and team","href":"#help?part=sign-in-and-team"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"My site is behind Cloudflare: will cached pages be missed?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Only if Skald reads nothing but your server's log. A page Cloudflare serves from its cache never reaches your server, so your server's log does not see that visit. Two fixes, set up by whoever runs your Skald server: Cloudflare's own request log (Logpush), if your Cloudflare plan offers it, or the small Skald Worker on any plan. The Worker sends Skald one line per request after the page has gone out, so it never slows the page. When Skald reads both the Worker and your server's log, it takes only the cached pages from the Worker, so no visit is counted twice."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"What does \"A newer Skald is available\" mean?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"A newer release of Skald is out than the one your server runs. Only owners and admins see this line at the top of the dashboard, and the daily and weekly mail show it too. "},{"b":"What's new"},{"s":" opens the release notes. "},{"b":"×"},{"s":" hides the line in your browser until the next release. A red line is a security release: ask whoever runs your Skald server to upgrade soon. Nothing changes until they do (or until they switch on automatic upgrades). To check, your server asks GitHub once a day which release is the latest; it sends only Skald's version, never your figures or visitors. Your server admin can turn this off ("},{"code":"updates.check: false"},{"s":"). See "},{"a":"Upgrading","href":"https://github.com/spcaeo/skald/blob/main/docs/UPGRADING.md"},{"s":"."}]},{"t":"h2","text":"How is Skald upgraded?"},{"t":"p","in":[{"s":"Whoever runs your Skald server upgrades it with one command. It checks the download, copies every database first, refuses to jump to a new major version or to run during the morning run, and puts the old version back if anything fails. Your figures and settings stay. Automatic upgrades for fixes (or fixes and features) can be switched on; they are off unless your admin turns them on. With Docker, the admin pulls the new image. See "},{"a":"Upgrading","href":"https://github.com/spcaeo/skald/blob/main/docs/UPGRADING.md"},{"s":"."}]}]}]};
